import Mathlib

/-!
# The four-dimensional coarse constants `κ ≤ 3321/500` and `C_coarse ≤ 10000/23851`, kernel-checked

This file certifies, with no floating-point input, the two finite constants of the depth-0 coarse
problem behind the four-dimensional aligned-cover estimate, on the coarse torus `(ℤ/4)⁴` (the case
`R = 2`). A floating-point and exact rational computation outside Lean proposes integer
certificates. The Lean kernel checks them by evaluating closed integer computations with
`decide +kernel`, and theorems proved once for every valid certificate turn a successful check
into a statement about real link fields.

**What is certified.**
* `kappa_bound`: `κ ≤ 3321/500`. For every box `b` of the coarse torus `(ℤ/4)⁴` and every field
  `φ` of its fibre `F_b⁽⁰⁾`, `∑_l φ_l² ≤ (3321/500) ∑_p (dφ)_p²`.
* `kappa_bound_norm`, `kappa_primitive`, `curv_injective_on_fibre` are the same bound in norm
  form: every `c ∈ K_b = d F_b⁽⁰⁾` has a fibre primitive with `|φ|² ≤ (3321/500) |c|²`, and `d` is
  injective on every fibre.
* `coarse_lower_bound`: `λ_min(∑_b Π_{K_b} | ℱ⁽⁰⁾) ≥ 23851/10000`. For every `x` in the curvature
  image `ℱ⁽⁰⁾ = d S⁽⁰⁾` of the section (`F0`), `(23851/10000) ‖x‖² ≤ ∑_b ‖Π_{K_b} x‖²`. The sum runs
  over all `256` boxes, and `Π_{K_b}` is the orthogonal projection onto `K_b` for the plain `ℓ²`
  norm on the `1536` plaquettes.
* `coarse_splitting`: `C_coarse^{4D} ≤ 10000/23851`. Every `c ∈ ℱ⁽⁰⁾` splits as `c = ∑_b c_b` with
  `c_b ∈ K_b` and `∑_b ‖c_b‖² ≤ (10000/23851) ‖c‖²`. Conversely, `coarse_lower_bound_of_splitting`
  recovers the lower bound from the splitting, so the splitting constant is `1 / λ_min`.
* `coarse_primitive_splitting` combines the two constants: every `c ∈ ℱ⁽⁰⁾` is `∑_b dφ_b` with
  `φ_b ∈ F_b⁽⁰⁾` and `∑_b |φ_b|² ≤ (3321/500) (10000/23851) ‖c‖²`.

None of these theorems has a hypothesis. Every closed fact they use is discharged in this file by
`decide +kernel`: `geomCheck`, `slotCheck`, the sixteen κ checks, `sectorCheck`, `zCheck` and the
sixteen sector checks.

**What is not certified here.**
* Only the coarse torus `(ℤ/4)⁴` (`R = 2`) is treated. Larger coarse tori have different constants
  and are not covered.
* Only the two bounds are proved, not the exact values. The exact values `κ = 6.6419143…`
  (attained in the class of the box at the origin) and `λ_min(∑_b Π_{K_b} | ℱ⁽⁰⁾) = 2.3851969684…`
  (attained in the sector `c = 4`, so `C_coarse = 0.4192526…`) come from the two independent exact
  computations outside Lean. The certified lower bound `23851/10000` lies about `9.7 · 10⁻⁵` below
  that `λ_min`.
* How the two constants enter the aligned-cover estimate is not formalised here.

## The problem, from the lattice (Section 2)

* Sites `s < 256` of `(ℤ/4)⁴`, links `4 s + μ` (`1024`), plaquettes `6 s + k` (`1536`).
* The plaquette operator is `curl`, the coboundary
  `(dφ)(s; μν) = φ(s,μ) + φ(s+e_μ,ν) − φ(s+e_ν,μ) − φ(s,ν)`.
* `isTree` gives the comb tree of the `2⁴` blocks: the link `(s, μ)` is frozen iff `x_ν` is
  even for every `ν ≥ μ`.
* `pinSum r` gives the `64` pins: sixteen times the coarse link variable `V(Z, μ)`, the average over
  the block `2Z + {0,1}⁴` of the two-step sums `φ(x, μ) + φ(x + e_μ, μ)`.
* `section0` is `S⁽⁰⁾`: tree links zero and all pins zero.
* `supported b` is the set of fields on the links with an endpoint in `b + {0,1}⁴`, and
  `fibre b = S⁽⁰⁾ ∩ supported b`.
* `curv` maps a field into `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1536)`, and `Kb b = curv (fibre b)`.

## The certificate (Sections 1 and 3)

* **Reduction to sixteen boxes.** Translations by `2t` preserve the tree and permute the pins,
  and every box is a translate of a box with corner in `{0,1}⁴`. The finite facts used are the
  closed checks `geomCheck` and `slotCheck`.
* **Slot coordinates.** The `96` links touching a box are numbered by slots and the `216`
  plaquettes with a vertex in it by patch slots. A fibre field is determined by its slot values,
  and its curvature on the patch is the local plaquette operator `dlocOf`.
* **Fibre parametrisation and spanning.** A matrix `Z = [I; C; 0]` has free, pivot and tree
  slots. Pin multipliers `W` with `W P = dW [−C | I]` show that every fibre field is `Z w`.
  The κ bound uses only this spanning property. `zCheck` (Section 4) also checks that the
  columns of `Z` lie in the fibre, so `Z` is a basis.
* **Packed LDLᵀ with a dominant remainder.** The form `σ (3321 Kᵀ K − 500 Zᵀ Z)`, `K = d Z`, is
  packed into one integer in base `2^K` (`pk`, with `pk_mul` for products). After subtracting
  `∑ₖ dₖ Mₖ ⊗ Mₖ`, the scan `psdScan` reads the remainder digit by digit and checks diagonal
  dominance. `qf_nonneg_of_psdScan` is its soundness theorem; it uses the injectivity of packing
  (`eq_zero_of_pk`) and the diagonal-dominance lemma `qf_nonneg_of_diagDom`.
* The kernel-evaluated functions use the core operations (`Nat.shiftLeft`, `Int.mul`, …), each
  with a lemma in ordinary notation.

## The coarse constant (Section 4)

* **Sectors.** The translations `τ_t` by `2t`, `t ∈ {0,1}⁴`, commute with `d`, preserve `S⁽⁰⁾`
  and permute the boxes. With the sixteen characters `χ_c(t) = (−1)^{#(c ∧ t)}` (`chiZ`), the
  sector parts `secL c φ = (1/16) ∑_t χ_c(t) φ ∘ τ_t` of a section field are section fields, add up
  to `φ` and have mutually orthogonal curvatures (`secL_mem`, `sum_secL`, `sum_sq_sectors`). The
  finite facts used are the closed check `sectorCheck`.
* **Sector coordinates.** A sector field is determined by its values on the `64` fundamental
  links. Twisted pins and an integer spanning certificate (`sBasis`) show that these values are
  `N y`, where `y` lists the values at `45` free fundamental links (`sector_value`). The curvature is
  then `E y` up to the character (`curl_cov`), with `E` the twisted plaquette operator times `N`.
* **Test fields.** For each class box `o` and sector `c` the certificate holds an integer matrix
  `Y_{o,c}`, and the slot field `Z_o Y_{o,c} y / 2^16` lies in the fibre of the class box
  (`testField_mem`). This uses `zCheck`: the columns of the κ parametrisation `Z_o` vanish on tree
  links and satisfy every pin, so `Z_o` is a basis of the fibre. The test field of the box
  `τ_t(o)` is `∑_c χ_c(t) (test field of (o, c)) ∘ τ_t` (`boxField`).
* **Variational bound.** `‖Π_K x‖² ≥ 2⟨x, k⟩ − ‖k‖²` for `k ∈ K` (`proj_lower`). Applied to the box
  test fields and summed over the `256` boxes, character orthogonality (`char_collapse`,
  `char_sq_collapse`) reduces `coarse_lower_bound` to one quadratic inequality in `45` variables
  per sector (`sector_ineq`, `coarse_of_certs`).
* **Sector certificates.** That inequality is `yᵀ H_c y ≥ 0` for the integer form
  `H_c = 10000 ∑_o ∑_q [2^16 (Ẽ ⊗ J + J ⊗ Ẽ) − J ⊗ J] − 23851 · 2^32 ∑ E ⊗ E` (`SCert.H`). The kernel
  recomputes `σ H_c` in packed form from the certificate (`pairAcc`, `SCert.Hpk_eq`) and checks a
  rounded `LDLᵀ` with a diagonally dominant remainder by the same `psdScan` as for κ
  (`sectorValid`, `sector_coord_ineq`).
* **Splitting.** `stable_splitting_of_lower` (the additive Schwarz lemma) turns the lower bound
  into the splitting, and `lower_of_stable_splitting` is its converse.

## Certificate sizes

* κ: the fibre dimensions of the sixteen class boxes (computed outside Lean) are 73, 60, 63, 48,
  65, 49, 51, 34, 66, 50, 52, 34, 54, 34, 34, 17. The LDLᵀ scale is `σ = 2^96` for the class of the
  box at the origin and `2^24` to `2^48` for the others.
* `C_coarse`: every sector has `45` free and `4` pivot fundamental links. The test-field matrices
  `Y_{o,c}` of a sector have `784` rows of `45` integers in all (absolute values below `2^17`, scale
  `2^16`). The packing base is `2^K` with `K = 132` to `171`. The LDLᵀ factors are rounded at `2^16`
  to `2^29`, and the form scale is `σ = 2^48` to `2^87` (`2^87` in the sharp sector `c = 4`).

## Non-vacuity

The section after the κ theorems builds a closed nonzero fibre field (`nvField`) and applies the κ
theorems to it. The section after the coarse theorems applies them to its curvature, which is a
nonzero element of `ℱ⁽⁰⁾` (`F0_ne_bot`). The last section applies the remaining lemmas with
hypotheses (`lcz_congr`, `trP_comp`, `trPlaq_comp`, `curl_secL`, `lower_of_stable_splitting`,
`coarse_lower_bound_of_splitting`) to concrete data.
-/

namespace Certified4DCoarse

open Finset


/-! ## 1. Generic certificates -/

section QuadForm

/-- The quadratic form `∑_{i<n} ∑_{j<n} H i j y i y j` of an `n × n` array. -/
def qf (n : ℕ) (H : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) (y : ℕ → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ i ∈ range n, ∑ j ∈ range n, H i j * y i * y j

theorem qf_add (n : ℕ) (H R : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) (y : ℕ → ℝ) :
    qf n (fun i j => H i j + R i j) y = qf n H y + qf n R y := by
  simp only [qf, add_mul, sum_add_distrib]

/-- **Diagonal dominance gives positivity.** If `R` is symmetric and every diagonal entry
dominates the off-diagonal absolute column sum, the quadratic form of `R` is nonnegative. -/
theorem qf_nonneg_of_diagDom {n : ℕ} {R : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ}
    (hsym : ∀ i < n, ∀ j < n, R i j = R j i)
    (hdom : ∀ j < n, ∑ i ∈ range n, (if i = j then 0 else |R i j|) ≤ R j j) (y : ℕ → ℝ) :
    0 ≤ qf n R y := by
  have hterm : ∀ i ∈ range n, ∀ j ∈ range n, (if i = j then R i i * y i ^ 2 else
      -(|R i j| / 2) * (y i ^ 2 + y j ^ 2)) ≤ R i j * y i * y j := by
    intro i _ j _
    split_ifs with h
    · subst h; ring_nf; exact le_refl _
    · have h1 : -(|R i j| * |y i * y j|) ≤ R i j * (y i * y j) := by
        have := neg_abs_le (R i j * (y i * y j))
        rw [abs_mul] at this; linarith
      have h2 : |y i * y j| ≤ (y i ^ 2 + y j ^ 2) / 2 := by
        rw [abs_mul]
        nlinarith [sq_nonneg (|y i| - |y j|), sq_abs (y i), sq_abs (y j)]
      have h3 : 0 ≤ |R i j| := abs_nonneg _
      nlinarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h2 h3]
  have hsum := sum_le_sum fun i hi => sum_le_sum fun j hj => hterm i hi j hj
  refine le_trans ?_ hsum
  have hsplit : ∀ i ∈ range n, ∑ j ∈ range n, (if i = j then R i i * y i ^ 2 else
      -(|R i j| / 2) * (y i ^ 2 + y j ^ 2)) =
      R i i * y i ^ 2 - (∑ j ∈ range n, (if i = j then 0 else |R i j| / 2)) * y i ^ 2 -
        ∑ j ∈ range n, (if i = j then 0 else |R i j| / 2 * y j ^ 2) := by
    intro i hi
    have e : ∀ j, (if i = j then R i i * y i ^ 2 else -(|R i j| / 2) * (y i ^ 2 + y j ^ 2)) =
        (if i = j then R i i * y i ^ 2 else 0) - (if i = j then 0 else |R i j| / 2) * y i ^ 2 -
          (if i = j then 0 else |R i j| / 2 * y j ^ 2) := by
      intro j; split_ifs <;> ring
    rw [sum_congr rfl fun j _ => e j, sum_sub_distrib, sum_sub_distrib, sum_ite_eq, ← sum_mul]
    simp [mem_range.mp hi]
  rw [sum_congr rfl hsplit, sum_sub_distrib, sum_sub_distrib]
  have hswap : ∑ i ∈ range n, ∑ j ∈ range n, (if i = j then (0 : ℝ) else |R i j| / 2 * y j ^ 2) =
      ∑ i ∈ range n, (∑ j ∈ range n, (if i = j then 0 else |R i j| / 2)) * y i ^ 2 := by
    rw [sum_comm]
    refine sum_congr rfl fun i hi => ?_
    rw [sum_mul]
    refine sum_congr rfl fun j hj => ?_
    by_cases h : j = i
    · subst h; simp
    · rw [if_neg h, if_neg (Ne.symm h), hsym j (mem_range.mp hj) i (mem_range.mp hi)]
  rw [hswap]
  have : ∀ i ∈ range n, 0 ≤ R i i * y i ^ 2 -
      2 * ((∑ j ∈ range n, (if i = j then 0 else |R i j| / 2)) * y i ^ 2) := by
    intro i hi
    have hd := hdom i (mem_range.mp hi)
    have : ∑ j ∈ range n, (if i = j then (0 : ℝ) else |R i j| / 2) =
        (∑ j ∈ range n, (if j = i then 0 else |R j i|)) / 2 := by
      rw [sum_div]
      refine sum_congr rfl fun j hj => ?_
      by_cases h : j = i
      · subst h; simp
      · rw [if_neg (Ne.symm h), if_neg h, hsym i (mem_range.mp hi) j (mem_range.mp hj)]
    rw [this]
    have := sq_nonneg (y i)
    nlinarith
  have h0 := sum_nonneg this
  rw [sum_sub_distrib, ← mul_sum] at h0
  linarith

/-- **LDLᵀ with a remainder.** If `H = ∑ₖ dₖ Mₖ Mₖᵀ + R` entrywise, then
`yᵀHy = ∑ₖ dₖ (Mₖ·y)² + yᵀRy`. -/
theorem qf_ldl {n m : ℕ} {H R M : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ} {d : ℕ → ℝ}
    (hH : ∀ i < n, ∀ j < n, H i j = ∑ k ∈ range m, d k * M k i * M k j + R i j) (y : ℕ → ℝ) :
    qf n H y = ∑ k ∈ range m, d k * (∑ i ∈ range n, M k i * y i) ^ 2 + qf n R y := by
  have : qf n H y = qf n (fun i j => ∑ k ∈ range m, d k * M k i * M k j) y + qf n R y := by
    rw [← qf_add]
    unfold qf
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun i hi => Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun j hj => ?_))
    rw [hH i (mem_range.mp hi) j (mem_range.mp hj)]
  rw [this]
  congr 1
  calc qf n (fun i j => ∑ k ∈ range m, d k * M k i * M k j) y
      = ∑ i ∈ range n, ∑ k ∈ range m, ∑ j ∈ range n, d k * M k i * M k j * y i * y j := by
        unfold qf
        refine sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
        simp only [sum_mul]
        exact sum_comm
    _ = ∑ k ∈ range m, ∑ i ∈ range n, ∑ j ∈ range n, d k * M k i * M k j * y i * y j := sum_comm
    _ = ∑ k ∈ range m, d k * (∑ i ∈ range n, M k i * y i) ^ 2 := by
        refine sum_congr rfl fun k _ => ?_
        rw [sq, sum_mul_sum, mul_sum]
        refine sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
        rw [mul_sum]
        refine sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
        ring

end QuadForm

section Packing

/-- **Packing.** `pk K n v = ∑_{j<n} v j · 2^(K j)`: the vector `v` read as one integer in base
`2^K`. -/
def pk (K n : ℕ) (v : ℕ → ℤ) : ℤ := ∑ j ∈ range n, v j * 2 ^ (K * j)

theorem pk_succ (K n : ℕ) (v : ℕ → ℤ) :
    pk K (n + 1) v = v 0 + 2 ^ K * pk K n (fun j => v (j + 1)) := by
  simp only [pk]
  rw [sum_range_succ', mul_sum]
  simp only [mul_zero, pow_zero, mul_one]
  rw [add_comm]
  congr 1
  refine sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
  rw [show K * (j + 1) = K + K * j by ring, pow_add]
  ring

/-- **Injectivity of packing.** If every entry is smaller than the base in absolute value and the
packed integer vanishes, then every entry vanishes. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_pk {K : ℕ} : ∀ {n : ℕ} {v : ℕ → ℤ}, (∀ j < n, |v j| < 2 ^ K) →
    pk K n v = 0 → ∀ j < n, v j = 0
  | 0, _, _, _, j, hj => absurd hj (Nat.not_lt_zero j)
  | n + 1, v, hv, h, j, hj => by
    rw [pk_succ] at h
    have h0 : v 0 = 0 := by
      have hd : (2 : ℤ) ^ K ∣ v 0 := ⟨-pk K n (fun j => v (j + 1)), by linarith⟩
      exact Int.eq_zero_of_abs_lt_dvd hd (hv 0 (Nat.succ_pos n))
    have hrest : pk K n (fun j => v (j + 1)) = 0 := by
      rw [h0, zero_add] at h
      rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h with h1 | h1
      · exact absurd h1 (by positivity)
      · exact h1
    cases j with
    | zero => exact h0
    | succ j =>
      exact eq_zero_of_pk (n := n) (v := fun j => v (j + 1))
        (fun i hi => hv (i + 1) (by omega)) hrest j (by omega)

theorem pk_sub (K n : ℕ) (u v : ℕ → ℤ) : pk K n (fun j => u j - v j) = pk K n u - pk K n v := by
  simp only [pk, sub_mul, sum_sub_distrib]

theorem pk_add (K n : ℕ) (u v : ℕ → ℤ) : pk K n (fun j => u j + v j) = pk K n u + pk K n v := by
  simp only [pk, add_mul, sum_add_distrib]

theorem pk_smul (K n : ℕ) (c : ℤ) (u : ℕ → ℤ) : pk K n (fun j => c * u j) = c * pk K n u := by
  simp only [pk, mul_sum, mul_assoc]

theorem pk_sum {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (K n : ℕ) (u : ι → ℕ → ℤ) :
    pk K n (fun j => ∑ t ∈ s, u t j) = ∑ t ∈ s, pk K n (u t) := by
  simp only [pk, sum_mul]
  exact sum_comm

theorem pk_congr {K n : ℕ} {u v : ℕ → ℤ} (h : ∀ j < n, u j = v j) : pk K n u = pk K n v :=
  sum_congr rfl fun j hj => by rw [h j (mem_range.mp hj)]

/-- **Products of packed rows.** Packing `u` in base `2^K` and `w` in base `2^(K n)` and
multiplying gives the packed outer product, with index `i + n j` for the entry `(i, j)`. -/
theorem pk_mul (K n : ℕ) (u w : ℕ → ℤ) :
    pk K n u * pk (K * n) n w = pk K (n * n) (fun t => u (t % n) * w (t / n)) := by
  simp only [pk]
  rw [sum_mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_product']
  symm
  refine Finset.sum_nbij' (fun t => (t % n, t / n)) (fun p => p.1 + n * p.2) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · intro t ht
    simp only [mem_range] at ht
    have hn : 0 < n := by
      rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with h | h
      · subst h; simp at ht
      · exact h
    simp only [mem_product, mem_range]
    exact ⟨Nat.mod_lt _ hn, Nat.div_lt_of_lt_mul ht⟩
  · intro p hp
    simp only [mem_product, mem_range] at hp
    simp only [mem_range]
    nlinarith [hp.1, hp.2]
  · intro t _
    exact Nat.mod_add_div t n
  · intro p hp
    simp only [mem_product, mem_range] at hp
    refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_
    · show (p.1 + n * p.2) % n = p.1
      rw [Nat.add_mul_mod_self_left, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hp.1]
    · show (p.1 + n * p.2) / n = p.2
      rw [Nat.add_mul_div_left _ _ (by omega), Nat.div_eq_of_lt hp.1, zero_add]
  · intro t _
    have : K * t = K * (t % n) + K * n * (t / n) := by
      conv_lhs => rw [← Nat.mod_add_div t n]
      ring
    rw [this, pow_add]
    ring

end Packing


/-! ### Kernel-evaluated arithmetic

The functions below are evaluated by the kernel. They are written with the core operations
(`Nat.add`, `Nat.shiftLeft`, `Int.mul`, …) rather than with the notation, so that the kernel
reaches the built-in arithmetic directly; each comes with a lemma in ordinary notation. -/

section DataRows

/-- Entry `j` of a signed data row `P` of width `w`: the `j`-th base-`2^w` digit of `P`, shifted
by `2^(w-1)`. -/
def ent (w P j : ℕ) : ℤ := (((P >>> (w * j)) % 2 ^ w : ℕ) : ℤ) - 2 ^ (w - 1)

/-- Entry `j` of an unsigned data row `P` of width `w`: the `j`-th base-`2^w` digit of `P`. -/
def uent (w P j : ℕ) : ℤ := (((P >>> (w * j)) % 2 ^ w : ℕ) : ℤ)

theorem abs_ent_le {w : ℕ} (hw : 1 ≤ w) (P j : ℕ) : |ent w P j| ≤ 2 ^ (w - 1) := by
  have h2 : (2 : ℤ) ^ w = 2 * 2 ^ (w - 1) := by
    rw [← pow_succ']; congr 1; omega
  have hlt : (((P >>> (w * j)) % 2 ^ w : ℕ) : ℤ) < 2 ^ w := by
    exact_mod_cast Nat.mod_lt _ (by positivity)
  have hnn : (0 : ℤ) ≤ (((P >>> (w * j)) % 2 ^ w : ℕ) : ℤ) := by positivity
  rw [abs_le]; unfold ent; constructor <;> linarith

theorem uent_nonneg (w P j : ℕ) : 0 ≤ uent w P j := by unfold uent; positivity

theorem uent_lt (w P j : ℕ) : uent w P j < 2 ^ w := by
  unfold uent; exact_mod_cast Nat.mod_lt _ (by positivity)

/-- The kernel form of `uent`. -/
def kuent (w P j : ℕ) : ℤ := Int.ofNat (Nat.mod (Nat.shiftRight P (Nat.mul w j)) (Nat.pow 2 w))

theorem kuent_eq (w P j : ℕ) : kuent w P j = uent w P j := rfl

/-- `∑_{j<n} (digit j of P) · 2^(K j)`, computed digit by digit. -/
def spreadU (w K P n : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  Nat.rec (motive := fun _ => ℕ) 0
    (fun j acc => Nat.add acc
      (Nat.shiftLeft (Nat.mod (Nat.shiftRight P (Nat.mul w j)) (Nat.pow 2 w)) (Nat.mul K j))) n

/-- `∑_{j<n} 2^(w-1) · 2^(K j)`. -/
def offs (w K n : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  Nat.rec (motive := fun _ => ℕ) 0
    (fun j acc => Nat.add acc (Nat.shiftLeft (Nat.pow 2 (Nat.sub w 1)) (Nat.mul K j))) n

/-- A signed data row repacked in base `2^K`. -/
def prow (w K n P : ℕ) : ℤ := Int.sub (Int.ofNat (spreadU w K P n)) (Int.ofNat (offs w K n))

/-- An unsigned data row repacked in base `2^K`. -/
def urow (w K n P : ℕ) : ℤ := Int.ofNat (spreadU w K P n)

theorem spreadU_eq (w K P n : ℕ) :
    (spreadU w K P n : ℤ) = ∑ j ∈ range n, (((P >>> (w * j)) % 2 ^ w : ℕ) : ℤ) * 2 ^ (K * j) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [spreadU]
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [sum_range_succ, ← ih]
    show ((spreadU w K P n + ((P >>> (w * n)) % 2 ^ w) <<< (K * n) : ℕ) : ℤ) = _
    rw [Nat.shiftLeft_eq]; push_cast; ring

theorem offs_eq (w K n : ℕ) :
    (offs w K n : ℤ) = ∑ j ∈ range n, (2 : ℤ) ^ (w - 1) * 2 ^ (K * j) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [offs]
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [sum_range_succ, ← ih]
    show ((offs w K n + 2 ^ (w - 1) <<< (K * n) : ℕ) : ℤ) = _
    rw [Nat.shiftLeft_eq]; push_cast; ring

theorem prow_eq (w K n P : ℕ) : prow w K n P = pk K n (ent w P) := by
  show (spreadU w K P n : ℤ) - (offs w K n : ℤ) = _
  rw [spreadU_eq, offs_eq, pk, ← sum_sub_distrib]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
  rw [ent]; ring

theorem urow_eq (w K n P : ℕ) : urow w K n P = pk K n (uent w P) := by
  show (spreadU w K P n : ℤ) = _
  rw [spreadU_eq, pk]; rfl

end DataRows

section Digits

/-- The balanced base-`2^K` digit of `x`, in `[-2^(K-1), 2^(K-1))`. -/
def bdig (K : ℕ) (x : ℤ) : ℤ :=
  Int.sub (Int.emod (Int.add x (Int.ofNat (Nat.pow 2 (Nat.sub K 1)))) (Int.ofNat (Nat.pow 2 K)))
    (Int.ofNat (Nat.pow 2 (Nat.sub K 1)))

/-- The quotient after removing the balanced digit. -/
def bnext (K : ℕ) (x : ℤ) : ℤ :=
  Int.ediv (Int.add x (Int.ofNat (Nat.pow 2 (Nat.sub K 1)))) (Int.ofNat (Nat.pow 2 K))

theorem bdig_def (K : ℕ) (x : ℤ) : bdig K x = (x + 2 ^ (K - 1)) % 2 ^ K - 2 ^ (K - 1) := by
  show (x + ((2 ^ (K - 1) : ℕ) : ℤ)) % ((2 ^ K : ℕ) : ℤ) - ((2 ^ (K - 1) : ℕ) : ℤ) = _
  push_cast; rfl

theorem bnext_def (K : ℕ) (x : ℤ) : bnext K x = (x + 2 ^ (K - 1)) / 2 ^ K := by
  show (x + ((2 ^ (K - 1) : ℕ) : ℤ)) / ((2 ^ K : ℕ) : ℤ) = _
  push_cast; rfl

theorem bdig_add (K : ℕ) (x : ℤ) : x = bdig K x + 2 ^ K * bnext K x := by
  have := Int.emod_add_ediv_mul (x + 2 ^ (K - 1)) (2 ^ K)
  rw [bdig_def, bnext_def]; linarith

theorem abs_bdig_le {K : ℕ} (hK : 1 ≤ K) (x : ℤ) : |bdig K x| ≤ 2 ^ (K - 1) := by
  have h2 : (2 : ℤ) ^ K = 2 * 2 ^ (K - 1) := by
    rw [← pow_succ']; congr 1; omega
  have hpos : (0 : ℤ) < 2 ^ K := by positivity
  have h0 := Int.emod_nonneg (x + 2 ^ (K - 1)) hpos.ne'
  have h1 := Int.emod_lt_of_pos (x + 2 ^ (K - 1)) hpos
  rw [abs_le, bdig_def]; constructor <;> linarith

/-- The `t`-th balanced digit of `x`. -/
def bdigs (K : ℕ) (x : ℤ) (t : ℕ) : ℤ := bdig K ((bnext K)^[t] x)

theorem pk_bdigs (K : ℕ) (x : ℤ) (N : ℕ) :
    x = pk K N (bdigs K x) + 2 ^ (K * N) * (bnext K)^[N] x := by
  induction N with
  | zero => simp [pk]
  | succ N ih =>
    have h := bdig_add K ((bnext K)^[N] x)
    have e : pk K (N + 1) (bdigs K x) =
        pk K N (bdigs K x) + bdig K ((bnext K)^[N] x) * 2 ^ (K * N) := by
      rw [pk, sum_range_succ, ← pk]; rfl
    rw [e, Function.iterate_succ_apply', show K * (N + 1) = K * N + K by ring, pow_add]
    linear_combination ih + (2 : ℤ) ^ (K * N) * h

theorem bdigs_iterate (K : ℕ) (x : ℤ) (a t : ℕ) :
    bdigs K ((bnext K)^[a] x) t = bdigs K x (a + t) := by
  unfold bdigs
  rw [← Function.iterate_add_apply, add_comm]

theorem abs_bdigs_le {K : ℕ} (hK : 1 ≤ K) (x : ℤ) (t : ℕ) : |bdigs K x t| ≤ 2 ^ (K - 1) :=
  abs_bdig_le hK _

/-- Forces the evaluation of an integer before passing it on (for kernel evaluation). -/
def forceZ {α : Sort*} (z : ℤ) (g : ℤ → α) : α :=
  Int.casesOn (motive := fun _ => α) z (fun k => g (Int.ofNat k)) (fun k => g (Int.negSucc k))

theorem forceZ_eq {α : Sort*} (z : ℤ) (g : ℤ → α) : forceZ z g = g z := by
  cases z <;> rfl

/-- The next `n` balanced digits of `x`, and the remaining quotient. -/
def takeCol (K : ℕ) (n : ℕ) : ℤ → List ℤ × ℤ :=
  Nat.rec (motive := fun _ => ℤ → List ℤ × ℤ) (fun x => ([], x))
    (fun _ rec x => let p := rec (bnext K x); (bdig K x :: p.1, p.2)) n

theorem takeCol_eq (K n : ℕ) (x : ℤ) :
    takeCol K n x = ((List.range n).map (bdigs K x), (bnext K)^[n] x) := by
  induction n generalizing x with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ n ih =>
    show (bdig K x :: (takeCol K n (bnext K x)).1, (takeCol K n (bnext K x)).2) = _
    rw [ih, List.range_succ_eq_map, List.map_cons, List.map_map]
    refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_
    · simp only [List.cons.injEq]
      refine ⟨rfl, List.map_congr_left fun t _ => ?_⟩
      simp only [Function.comp_apply]
      rw [show bnext K x = (bnext K)^[1] x from rfl, bdigs_iterate, add_comm]
    · show (bnext K)^[n] (bnext K x) = (bnext K)^[n + 1] x
      rw [Function.iterate_succ_apply]

theorem sum_range_eq_list (f : ℕ → ℤ) (n : ℕ) :
    ∑ i ∈ range n, f i = ((List.range n).map f).sum := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp
  | succ n ih => rw [sum_range_succ, ih, List.range_succ, List.map_append, List.sum_append]; simp

/-- Absolute value, in kernel form. -/
def iabs (x : ℤ) : ℤ := Int.ofNat x.natAbs

theorem iabs_eq (x : ℤ) : iabs x = |x| := Int.natCast_natAbs x

/-- Sum of a list of integers, in kernel form. -/
def lsum : List ℤ → ℤ
  | [] => 0
  | a :: as => Int.add a (lsum as)

theorem lsum_eq : ∀ l : List ℤ, lsum l = l.sum
  | [] => rfl
  | a :: as => by rw [lsum, List.sum_cons, ← lsum_eq as]; rfl

/-- **Column dominance**: the `j`-th entry of the column dominates the sum of the absolute values
of the other entries. -/
def colOK (j : ℕ) (ds : List ℤ) : Bool :=
  @decide (Int.sub (lsum (ds.map iabs)) (iabs (ds.getD j 0)) ≤ ds.getD j 0) (Int.decLe _ _)

theorem colOK_iff (j : ℕ) (ds : List ℤ) :
    colOK j ds = true ↔ (ds.map abs).sum - |ds.getD j 0| ≤ ds.getD j 0 := by
  unfold colOK
  rw [decide_eq_true_iff]
  have e : ds.map iabs = ds.map abs := List.map_congr_left fun x _ => iabs_eq x
  rw [e, lsum_eq, iabs_eq]; rfl

/-- **The PSD scan.** It reads `x` as an `n × n` array of balanced base-`2^K` digits, one column of
`n` digits (a base-`2^(K n)` digit of `x`) at a time. It checks that each column decomposes
exactly into its `n` digits, that the column is dominated by its diagonal entry, and that
nothing is left over. -/
def psdScan (K n : ℕ) (f : ℕ) : ℕ → ℤ → Bool :=
  Nat.rec (motive := fun _ => ℕ → ℤ → Bool) (fun _ x => decide (x = 0))
    (fun _ rec j x =>
      let p := takeCol K n (bdig (K * n) x)
      decide (p.2 = 0) && colOK j p.1 && forceZ (bnext (K * n) x) (rec (j + 1))) f

theorem psdScan_sound (K n : ℕ) : ∀ (f j : ℕ) (x : ℤ), psdScan K n f j x = true →
    (∀ c < f, (bnext K)^[n] (bdigs (K * n) x c) = 0 ∧
      colOK (j + c) ((List.range n).map (bdigs K (bdigs (K * n) x c))) = true) ∧
      (bnext (K * n))^[f] x = 0
  | 0, j, x, h => by
    refine ⟨fun c hc => absurd hc (Nat.not_lt_zero c), ?_⟩
    simpa [psdScan] using h
  | f + 1, j, x, h => by
    have h' : (decide ((takeCol K n (bdig (K * n) x)).2 = 0) &&
        colOK j (takeCol K n (bdig (K * n) x)).1 &&
        psdScan K n f (j + 1) (bnext (K * n) x)) = true := by
      have e : psdScan K n (f + 1) j x =
          (decide ((takeCol K n (bdig (K * n) x)).2 = 0) &&
            colOK j (takeCol K n (bdig (K * n) x)).1 &&
            forceZ (bnext (K * n) x) (psdScan K n f (j + 1))) := rfl
      rw [e, forceZ_eq] at h
      exact h
    rw [takeCol_eq] at h'
    simp only [Bool.and_eq_true, decide_eq_true_eq] at h'
    obtain ⟨⟨h0, h1⟩, h2⟩ := h'
    obtain ⟨ih1, ih2⟩ := psdScan_sound K n f (j + 1) _ h2
    refine ⟨fun c hc => ?_, ?_⟩
    · rcases c with _ | c
      · exact ⟨h0, h1⟩
      · have := ih1 c (by omega)
        rw [show bnext (K * n) x = (bnext (K * n))^[1] x from rfl, bdigs_iterate,
          show 1 + c = c + 1 by ring] at this
        rw [show j + (c + 1) = j + 1 + c by ring]
        exact this
    · rw [Function.iterate_succ_apply]
      exact ih2

/-- Nested packing: packing the packed columns in base `2^(K n)` is packing the whole array in
base `2^K`, with index `i + n c` for the entry `i` of the column `c`. -/
theorem pk_nested (K n f : ℕ) (D : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ) :
    pk (K * n) f (fun c => pk K n (D c)) = pk K (n * f) (fun t => D (t / n) (t % n)) := by
  simp only [pk, sum_mul]
  rw [← Finset.sum_product']
  symm
  refine Finset.sum_nbij' (fun t => (t / n, t % n)) (fun p => p.2 + n * p.1) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · intro t ht
    simp only [mem_range] at ht
    have hn : 0 < n := by
      rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with h | h
      · subst h; simp at ht
      · exact h
    simp only [mem_product, mem_range]
    exact ⟨Nat.div_lt_of_lt_mul ht, Nat.mod_lt _ hn⟩
  · intro p hp
    simp only [mem_product, mem_range] at hp
    simp only [mem_range]
    nlinarith [hp.1, hp.2]
  · intro t _
    show t % n + n * (t / n) = t
    exact Nat.mod_add_div t n
  · intro p hp
    simp only [mem_product, mem_range] at hp
    refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_
    · show (p.2 + n * p.1) / n = p.1
      rw [Nat.add_mul_div_left _ _ (by omega), Nat.div_eq_of_lt hp.2, zero_add]
    · show (p.2 + n * p.1) % n = p.2
      rw [Nat.add_mul_mod_self_left, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hp.2]
  · intro t _
    have : K * t = K * (t % n) + K * n * (t / n) := by
      conv_lhs => rw [← Nat.mod_add_div t n]
      ring
    rw [this, pow_add]
    ring

end Digits

section PSDCheck

/-- `∑ₖ dₖ (Mₖ ⊗ Mₖ)` in packed form, for the rows `Mₖ` of `Ms` (width `wM`) and the unsigned
weights `dₖ` (width `wd`) of `dP`, starting at weight index `k`. -/
def ldlSum (K n wM wd dP : ℕ) : List ℕ → ℕ → ℤ
  | [], _ => 0
  | P :: Ps, k => Int.add (Int.mul (Int.mul (kuent wd dP k) (prow wM K n P))
      (prow wM (Nat.mul K n) n P)) (ldlSum K n wM wd dP Ps (k + 1))

theorem ldlSum_eq (K n wM wd dP : ℕ) : ∀ (Ms : List ℕ) (k0 : ℕ),
    ldlSum K n wM wd dP Ms k0 = pk K (n * n) (fun t => ∑ k ∈ range Ms.length,
      uent wd dP (k0 + k) * (ent wM (Ms.getD k 0) (t % n) * ent wM (Ms.getD k 0) (t / n)))
  | [], k0 => by simp [ldlSum, pk]
  | P :: Ps, k0 => by
    show uent wd dP k0 * prow wM K n P * prow wM (K * n) n P + ldlSum K n wM wd dP Ps (k0 + 1) = _
    rw [ldlSum_eq K n wM wd dP Ps (k0 + 1), prow_eq, prow_eq, mul_assoc, pk_mul,
      ← pk_smul, ← pk_add]
    refine pk_congr fun t _ => ?_
    rw [List.length_cons, sum_range_succ']
    simp only [List.getD_cons_zero, List.getD_cons_succ, add_zero]
    rw [add_comm]
    congr 1
    refine sum_congr rfl fun k _ => ?_
    rw [show k0 + 1 + k = k0 + (k + 1) by ring]

/-- **Soundness of the packed PSD check.** Let `H` be a symmetric integer `n × n` array with
entries bounded by `βH`, packed with index `i + n j`. If the scan of `pk(H) − ∑ₖ dₖ Mₖ ⊗ Mₖ`
succeeds and the base `2^K` is large enough, then the quadratic form of `H` is nonnegative. -/
theorem qf_nonneg_of_psdScan {K n wM wd dP βH : ℕ} {Ms : List ℕ} {H : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ}
    (hK : 1 ≤ K) (hwM : 1 ≤ wM)
    (hsym : ∀ i < n, ∀ j < n, H i j = H j i) (hb : ∀ i < n, ∀ j < n, |H i j| ≤ βH)
    (hbig : 2 * (βH + Ms.length * 2 ^ wd * 2 ^ (wM - 1) * 2 ^ (wM - 1)) < 2 ^ K)
    (hscan : psdScan K n n 0 (pk K (n * n) (fun t => H (t % n) (t / n)) -
      ldlSum K n wM wd dP Ms 0) = true) (y : ℕ → ℝ) :
    0 ≤ qf n (fun i j => (H i j : ℝ)) y := by
  set x := pk K (n * n) (fun t => H (t % n) (t / n)) - ldlSum K n wM wd dP Ms 0 with hx
  obtain ⟨hcol, hrest⟩ := psdScan_sound K n n 0 x hscan
  set m := Ms.length
  set D : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ := fun i j => ∑ k ∈ range m,
    uent wd dP k * (ent wM (Ms.getD k 0) i * ent wM (Ms.getD k 0) j) with hD
  set E : ℕ → ℤ := fun t => bdigs K (bdigs (K * n) x (t / n)) (t % n) with hE
  have hx2 : x = pk K (n * n) E := by
    have h1 := pk_bdigs (K * n) x n
    rw [hrest, mul_zero, add_zero] at h1
    have h2 : ∀ c < n, bdigs (K * n) x c = pk K n (bdigs K (bdigs (K * n) x c)) := by
      intro c hc
      have := pk_bdigs K (bdigs (K * n) x c) n
      rw [(hcol c hc).1, mul_zero, add_zero] at this
      exact this
    rw [h1, pk_congr h2, pk_nested]
  have hdiff : pk K (n * n) (fun t => H (t % n) (t / n) - D (t % n) (t / n) - E t) = 0 := by
    rw [pk_sub, pk_sub, ← hx2]
    have := ldlSum_eq K n wM wd dP Ms 0
    simp only [zero_add] at this
    rw [hx, this]
    ring
  have hbd : ∀ t < n * n, |H (t % n) (t / n) - D (t % n) (t / n) - E t| < 2 ^ K := by
    intro t ht
    have hn : 0 < n := by
      rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with h | h
      · subst h; simp at ht
      · exact h
    have hi : t % n < n := Nat.mod_lt _ hn
    have hj : t / n < n := Nat.div_lt_of_lt_mul ht
    have h1 := hb _ hi _ hj
    have h2 : |D (t % n) (t / n)| ≤ m * 2 ^ wd * 2 ^ (wM - 1) * 2 ^ (wM - 1) := by
      rw [hD]
      refine (abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans ?_
      have : ∀ k ∈ range m, |uent wd dP k * (ent wM (Ms.getD k 0) (t % n) *
          ent wM (Ms.getD k 0) (t / n))| ≤ 2 ^ wd * 2 ^ (wM - 1) * 2 ^ (wM - 1) := by
        intro k _
        rw [abs_mul, abs_mul, mul_assoc]
        refine mul_le_mul ?_ (mul_le_mul (abs_ent_le hwM _ _) (abs_ent_le hwM _ _)
          (abs_nonneg _) (by positivity)) (by positivity) (by positivity)
        rw [abs_of_nonneg (uent_nonneg _ _ _)]; exact (uent_lt _ _ _).le
      refine (sum_le_sum this).trans ?_
      rw [sum_const, card_range, nsmul_eq_mul]; ring_nf; exact le_refl _
    have h3 := abs_bdigs_le hK (bdigs (K * n) x (t / n)) (t % n)
    have h4 : (2 : ℤ) ^ K = 2 * 2 ^ (K - 1) := by rw [← pow_succ']; congr 1; omega
    have hbig' : 2 * ((βH : ℤ) + m * 2 ^ wd * 2 ^ (wM - 1) * 2 ^ (wM - 1)) < 2 ^ K := by
      exact_mod_cast hbig
    have b1 := abs_le.mp h1
    have b2 := abs_le.mp h2
    have b3 := abs_le.mp h3
    rw [abs_lt]
    constructor <;> linarith [b1.1, b1.2, b2.1, b2.2, b3.1, b3.2]
  have hR := eq_zero_of_pk hbd hdiff
  have hRij : ∀ i < n, ∀ j < n, H i j - D i j = bdigs K (bdigs (K * n) x j) i := by
    intro i hi j hj
    have := hR (i + n * j) (by nlinarith)
    have e1 : (i + n * j) % n = i := by rw [Nat.add_mul_mod_self_left, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hi]
    have e2 : (i + n * j) / n = j := by
      rw [Nat.add_mul_div_left _ _ (by omega), Nat.div_eq_of_lt hi, zero_add]
    simp only [hE, e1, e2] at this
    linarith
  set R : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ := fun i j => ((H i j - D i j : ℤ) : ℝ) with hRdef
  have hDsym : ∀ i j, D i j = D j i := by
    intro i j; rw [hD]; exact sum_congr rfl fun k _ => by ring
  have hRsym : ∀ i < n, ∀ j < n, R i j = R j i := by
    intro i hi j hj; simp only [hRdef]; rw [hsym i hi j hj, hDsym]
  have hRdom : ∀ j < n, ∑ i ∈ range n, (if i = j then 0 else |R i j|) ≤ R j j := by
    intro j hj
    set c := bdigs (K * n) x j
    have hc := (colOK_iff _ _).mp (hcol j hj).2
    simp only [zero_add] at hc
    have hlist : ((List.range n).map (bdigs K c)).getD j 0 = bdigs K c j := by
      rw [List.getD_eq_getElem?_getD, List.getElem?_map, List.getElem?_range hj]; rfl
    rw [hlist, List.map_map, ← sum_range_eq_list] at hc
    have hRj : ∀ i < n, R i j = (bdigs K c i : ℝ) := by
      intro i hi; simp only [hRdef]; rw [hRij i hi j hj]
    have e : ∑ i ∈ range n, |R i j| =
        ∑ i ∈ range n, (if i = j then 0 else |R i j|) + |R j j| := by
      have : ∑ i ∈ range n, |R i j| = ∑ i ∈ range n, ((if i = j then 0 else |R i j|) +
          (if i = j then |R i j| else 0)) := sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by split_ifs <;> simp
      rw [this, sum_add_distrib, sum_ite_eq']
      simp [mem_range.mpr hj]
    have e2 : ∑ i ∈ range n, |R i j| = ((∑ i ∈ range n, |bdigs K c i| : ℤ) : ℝ) := by
      push_cast
      exact sum_congr rfl fun i hi => by rw [hRj i (mem_range.mp hi)]
    have hc' : ((∑ i ∈ range n, |bdigs K c i| : ℤ) : ℝ) - |(bdigs K c j : ℝ)|
        ≤ (bdigs K c j : ℝ) := by
      have := (Int.cast_le (R := ℝ)).mpr hc
      push_cast at this ⊢
      simpa [Function.comp_def] using this
    rw [hRj j hj]
    rw [hRj j hj] at e
    linarith
  have hHR : ∀ i < n, ∀ j < n, (H i j : ℝ) =
      ∑ k ∈ range m, (uent wd dP k : ℝ) * (ent wM (Ms.getD k 0) i : ℝ) *
        (ent wM (Ms.getD k 0) j : ℝ) + R i j := by
    intro i _ j _
    simp only [hRdef, hD]
    push_cast
    rw [sub_eq_neg_add, ← add_assoc]
    simp only [mul_assoc]
    ring
  rw [qf_ldl hHR y]
  refine add_nonneg (sum_nonneg fun k _ => mul_nonneg ?_ (sq_nonneg _))
    (qf_nonneg_of_diagDom hRsym hRdom y)
  exact_mod_cast uent_nonneg _ _ _

end PSDCheck


/-! ## 2. The four-dimensional depth-0 coarse problem

The coarse torus is `(ℤ/4)⁴`. A site is a number `s < 256` with coordinates
`s = ((x₀ · 4 + x₁) · 4 + x₂) · 4 + x₃`; the link from `s` in direction `μ < 4` is `4 s + μ`
(`1024` links); the plaquette at `s` in the plane `k < 6` is `6 s + k` (`1536` plaquettes), with the
planes `(0,1), (0,2), (0,3), (1,2), (1,3), (2,3)` in this order. -/

section Lattice

/-- Coordinate `a < 4` of the site `s`: `s / 4^(3-a) mod 4`. -/
def coord (s a : ℕ) : ℕ := s / (if a = 0 then 64 else if a = 1 then 16 else if a = 2 then 4 else 1) % 4

/-- The site with coordinates `x₀, x₁, x₂, x₃` (read modulo `4`). -/
def site4 (x₀ x₁ x₂ x₃ : ℕ) : ℕ := ((x₀ % 4 * 4 + x₁ % 4) * 4 + x₂ % 4) * 4 + x₃ % 4

/-- The site `s + e_a`. -/
def step (s a : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  site4 (coord s 0 + if a = 0 then 1 else 0) (coord s 1 + if a = 1 then 1 else 0)
    (coord s 2 + if a = 2 then 1 else 0) (coord s 3 + if a = 3 then 1 else 0)

/-- The site `s - e_a`. -/
def back (s a : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  site4 (coord s 0 + if a = 0 then 3 else 0) (coord s 1 + if a = 1 then 3 else 0)
    (coord s 2 + if a = 2 then 3 else 0) (coord s 3 + if a = 3 then 3 else 0)

/-- The first direction `μ` of the plane `k`. -/
def planeMu (k : ℕ) : ℕ := [0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2].getD k 0

/-- The second direction `ν` of the plane `k`. -/
def planeNu (k : ℕ) : ℕ := [1, 2, 3, 2, 3, 3].getD k 0

/-- The `i`-th link of the plaquette `p = 6 s + k` in the plane `(μ, ν)`:
`(s, μ)`, `(s + e_μ, ν)`, `(s + e_ν, μ)`, `(s, ν)`. -/
def plaqLink (p i : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  let s := p / 6
  let μ := planeMu (p % 6)
  let ν := planeNu (p % 6)
  if i = 0 then 4 * s + μ else if i = 1 then 4 * step s μ + ν
  else if i = 2 then 4 * step s ν + μ else 4 * s + ν

/-- The link with index `n` (reduced modulo `1024`). -/
def fl (n : ℕ) : Fin 1024 := ⟨n % 1024, Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num)⟩

/-- **The plaquette operator** (the coboundary `d`):
`(d φ)(s; μν) = φ(s, μ) + φ(s + e_μ, ν) − φ(s + e_ν, μ) − φ(s, ν)`. -/
def curl (φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ) (p : Fin 1536) : ℝ :=
  φ (fl (plaqLink p 0)) + φ (fl (plaqLink p 1)) - φ (fl (plaqLink p 2)) - φ (fl (plaqLink p 3))

/-- **Tree links** (the comb tree of the `2⁴` blocks): the link `(s, μ)` is frozen iff `x_ν` is
even for every `ν ≥ μ`. -/
def isTree (l : ℕ) : Bool :=
  (!decide (l % 4 ≤ 0) || decide (coord (l / 4) 0 % 2 = 0)) &&
  (!decide (l % 4 ≤ 1) || decide (coord (l / 4) 1 % 2 = 0)) &&
  (!decide (l % 4 ≤ 2) || decide (coord (l / 4) 2 % 2 = 0)) &&
  decide (coord (l / 4) 3 % 2 = 0)

/-- Bit `a < 4` of a number `Z < 16`, most significant first: `Z / 2^(3-a) mod 2`. -/
def bit (Z a : ℕ) : ℕ := Z / (if a = 0 then 8 else if a = 1 then 4 else if a = 2 then 2 else 1) % 2

/-- The site `2 Z + o` of the block `Z` (`Z, o < 16`, read as bit vectors). -/
def blockSite (Z o : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  site4 (2 * bit Z 0 + bit o 0) (2 * bit Z 1 + bit o 1) (2 * bit Z 2 + bit o 2)
    (2 * bit Z 3 + bit o 3)

/-- **The pins.** Row `r = 16 μ + Z` is sixteen times the coarse link variable `V(Z, μ)`, the average
over `x ∈ 2 Z + {0, 1}⁴` of the two-step sums: `∑_{x ∈ 2Z + {0,1}⁴} (φ(x, μ) + φ(x + e_μ, μ))`. -/
def pinSum (r : Fin 64) (φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ o : Fin 16, (φ (fl (4 * blockSite (r % 16) o + r / 16)) +
    φ (fl (4 * step (blockSite (r % 16) o) (r / 16) + r / 16)))

/-- Whether the site `s` lies in the box `b + {0, 1}⁴`. -/
def inBox (b s : ℕ) : Bool :=
  decide ((coord s 0 + 4 - coord b 0) % 4 < 2) && decide ((coord s 1 + 4 - coord b 1) % 4 < 2) &&
    decide ((coord s 2 + 4 - coord b 2) % 4 < 2) && decide ((coord s 3 + 4 - coord b 3) % 4 < 2)

/-- Whether the link `l` has an endpoint in the box `b + {0, 1}⁴`. -/
def touches (b l : ℕ) : Bool := inBox b (l / 4) || inBox b (step (l / 4) (l % 4))

/-- **The section** `S⁽⁰⁾`: link fields vanishing on the tree links, with all `64` pins zero. -/
def section0 : Submodule ℝ (Fin 1024 → ℝ) where
  carrier := {φ | (∀ l : Fin 1024, isTree l = true → φ l = 0) ∧ ∀ r : Fin 64, pinSum r φ = 0}
  add_mem' := by
    rintro φ ψ ⟨h1, h2⟩ ⟨h3, h4⟩
    refine ⟨fun l hl => by simp [h1 l hl, h3 l hl], fun r => ?_⟩
    have e : pinSum r (φ + ψ) = pinSum r φ + pinSum r ψ := by
      simp only [pinSum, Pi.add_apply, ← sum_add_distrib]
      exact sum_congr rfl fun o _ => by ring
    rw [e, h2 r, h4 r, add_zero]
  zero_mem' := ⟨fun _ _ => rfl, fun r => by simp [pinSum]⟩
  smul_mem' := by
    rintro c φ ⟨h1, h2⟩
    refine ⟨fun l hl => by simp [h1 l hl], fun r => ?_⟩
    have e : pinSum r (c • φ) = c * pinSum r φ := by
      simp only [pinSum, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, mul_sum]
      exact sum_congr rfl fun o _ => by ring
    rw [e, h2 r, mul_zero]

theorem mem_section0 {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ} :
    φ ∈ section0 ↔ (∀ l : Fin 1024, isTree l = true → φ l = 0) ∧ ∀ r : Fin 64, pinSum r φ = 0 :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- Link fields supported on the links touching the box `b + {0, 1}⁴`. -/
def supported (b : ℕ) : Submodule ℝ (Fin 1024 → ℝ) where
  carrier := {φ | ∀ l : Fin 1024, touches b l = false → φ l = 0}
  add_mem' := by
    intro φ ψ hφ hψ l hl
    simp [hφ l hl, hψ l hl]
  zero_mem' := fun _ _ => rfl
  smul_mem' := by
    intro c φ hφ l hl
    simp [hφ l hl]

theorem mem_supported {b : ℕ} {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ} :
    φ ∈ supported b ↔ ∀ l : Fin 1024, touches b l = false → φ l = 0 := Iff.rfl

/-- **The fibre** `F_b⁽⁰⁾` of the box `b`: section fields supported on the links touching it. -/
def fibre (b : ℕ) : Submodule ℝ (Fin 1024 → ℝ) := section0 ⊓ supported b

/-- **The curvature map** `φ ↦ dφ`, into the Euclidean space of the `1536` plaquettes. -/
noncomputable def curv : (Fin 1024 → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1536) where
  toFun φ := WithLp.toLp 2 (curl φ)
  map_add' φ ψ := by
    rw [← WithLp.toLp_add]; congr 1; ext p; simp only [curl, Pi.add_apply]; ring
  map_smul' c φ := by
    rw [RingHom.id_apply, ← WithLp.toLp_smul]; congr 1; ext p
    simp only [curl, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]; ring

/-- **The curvature fibre** `K_b = d F_b⁽⁰⁾` of the box `b`. -/
noncomputable def Kb (b : Fin 256) : Submodule ℝ (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1536)) :=
  (fibre b).map curv

end Lattice


/-! ### Translations and the box geometry

Translations by `2t` (`t < 16`, read as a bit vector) preserve the tree links and permute the
pins; every box is a translate of one of the sixteen boxes with corner in `{0, 1}⁴`. The `96`
links touching the box with corner `b` are numbered by slots, the `216` plaquettes with a vertex in
the box by patch slots, both relative to `b`. All finite facts are closed Boolean computations,
checked by the kernel. -/

section Geometry

/-- `f i = true` for every `i < n` (a kernel-friendly bounded quantifier). -/
def allBelow (n : ℕ) (f : ℕ → Bool) : Bool :=
  Nat.rec (motive := fun _ => Bool) true (fun i acc => f i && acc) n

theorem allBelow_iff {n : ℕ} {f : ℕ → Bool} : allBelow n f = true ↔ ∀ i < n, f i = true := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [allBelow]
  | succ n ih =>
    show (f n && allBelow n f) = true ↔ _
    rw [Bool.and_eq_true, ih]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩ i hi
      rcases Nat.lt_succ_iff_lt_or_eq.mp hi with h | h
      · exact h2 i h
      · subst h; exact h1
    · intro h
      exact ⟨h n (Nat.lt_succ_self n), fun i hi => h i (Nat.lt_succ_of_lt hi)⟩

/-- The translation `s ↦ s + 2t` of sites. -/
def trSite (t s : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  site4 (coord s 0 + 2 * bit t 0) (coord s 1 + 2 * bit t 1) (coord s 2 + 2 * bit t 2)
    (coord s 3 + 2 * bit t 3)

/-- The translation of links. -/
def trL (t l : ℕ) : ℕ := 4 * trSite t (l / 4) + l % 4

/-- The translation of plaquettes. -/
def trP (t p : ℕ) : ℕ := 6 * trSite t (p / 6) + p % 6

/-- The corner of the class box `o < 16`: the site whose coordinates are the bits of `o`. -/
def corner (o : ℕ) : ℕ := site4 (bit o 0) (bit o 1) (bit o 2) (bit o 3)

/-- The class of the box `b`: the parities of its coordinates. -/
def clsOf (b : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  8 * (coord b 0 % 2) + 4 * (coord b 1 % 2) + 2 * (coord b 2 % 2) + coord b 3 % 2

/-- The translation taking the class box of `b` to `b`. -/
def trOf (b : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  8 * (coord b 0 / 2) + 4 * (coord b 1 / 2) + 2 * (coord b 2 / 2) + coord b 3 / 2

/-- Relative offset (mod 4) in direction `a` of the slot `s = 24 μ + 8 e + r`: `e - 1` in
direction `μ`, and the bits of `r` in the other three directions (in increasing order). -/
def slotOff (s a : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  if a = s / 24 then s / 8 % 3 + 3
  else s % 8 / Nat.pow 2 (2 - (if a < s / 24 then a else a - 1)) % 2

/-- The link of the slot `s < 96` of the box with corner `b`. -/
def slotLink (b s : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  4 * site4 (coord b 0 + slotOff s 0) (coord b 1 + slotOff s 1) (coord b 2 + slotOff s 2)
    (coord b 3 + slotOff s 3) + s / 24

/-- The slot of a link touching the box with corner `b`. -/
def slotOf (b l : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  let rel := fun a => (coord (l / 4) a + 4 - coord b a) % 4
  let acc := fun acc a => if a = l % 4 then acc else 2 * acc + rel a
  24 * (l % 4) + 8 * ((rel (l % 4) + 1) % 4) + acc (acc (acc (acc 0 0) 1) 2) 3

/-- Relative offset in direction `a` of the patch slot `q = 36 k + 12 e + 4 f + r` (plane
`k = (m, n)`): `e - 1` in direction `m`, `f - 1` in direction `n`, the bits of `r` in the other
two directions. -/
def patchOff (q a : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  if a = planeMu (q / 36) then q / 12 % 3 + 3
  else if a = planeNu (q / 36) then q / 4 % 3 + 3
  else q % 4 / Nat.pow 2 (1 - (a - (if planeMu (q / 36) < a then 1 else 0) -
    (if planeNu (q / 36) < a then 1 else 0))) % 2

/-- The plaquette of the patch slot `q < 216` of the box with corner `b`. -/
def patchPlaq (b q : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  6 * site4 (coord b 0 + patchOff q 0) (coord b 1 + patchOff q 1) (coord b 2 + patchOff q 2)
    (coord b 3 + patchOff q 3) + q / 36

/-- The patch slot of a plaquette with a vertex in the box with corner `b`. -/
def patchOf (b p : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  let rel := fun a => (coord (p / 6) a + 4 - coord b a) % 4
  let m := planeMu (p % 6)
  let n := planeNu (p % 6)
  let acc := fun acc a => if a = m ∨ a = n then acc else 2 * acc + rel a
  36 * (p % 6) + 12 * ((rel m + 1) % 4) + 4 * ((rel n + 1) % 4) +
    acc (acc (acc (acc 0 0) 1) 2) 3

/-- The plane of the directions `μ ≠ ν`. -/
def planeIdx (μ ν : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  if min μ ν = 0 then max μ ν - 1 else if min μ ν = 1 then max μ ν + 1 else 5

/-- The six plaquettes containing the link `l`. -/
def plaqsOf (l : ℕ) : List ℕ :=
  (List.range 4).flatMap fun ν => if ν = l % 4 then [] else
    [6 * (l / 4) + planeIdx (l % 4) ν, 6 * back (l / 4) ν + planeIdx (l % 4) ν]

/-- **Finite facts about the torus**, one Boolean computation. -/
def geomCheck : Bool :=
  -- translations: involutions, compatible with steps and coordinates, preserving tree links
  allBelow 16 (fun t => allBelow 256 (fun s =>
    trSite t (trSite t s) == s && trSite t s < 256 &&
    allBelow 4 (fun a => step (trSite t s) a == trSite t (step s a) &&
      coord (trSite t s) a == (coord s a + 2 * bit t a) % 4))) &&
  allBelow 16 (fun t => allBelow 1024 (fun l => isTree (trL t l) == isTree l)) &&
  allBelow 16 (fun t => allBelow 16 (fun Z => allBelow 16 (fun o =>
    trSite t (blockSite Z o) == blockSite (Z ^^^ t) o))) &&
  -- every box is the translate of its class box
  allBelow 256 (fun b => trSite (trOf b) (corner (clsOf b)) == b && clsOf b < 16 && trOf b < 16) &&
  -- steps stay on the torus
  allBelow 256 (fun s => allBelow 4 (fun a => step s a < 256)) &&
  -- every plaquette lies in the plaquette list of each of its links
  allBelow 1536 (fun p => allBelow 4 (fun i => (plaqsOf (plaqLink p i)).contains p &&
    plaqLink p i < 1024))

/-- **Finite facts about the slots of the sixteen class boxes**, one Boolean computation. -/
def slotCheck : Bool :=
  allBelow 16 fun o =>
    allBelow 96 (fun s => slotLink (corner o) s < 1024 && touches (corner o) (slotLink (corner o) s)
      && slotOf (corner o) (slotLink (corner o) s) == s) &&
    allBelow 1024 (fun l => !touches (corner o) l ||
      (slotOf (corner o) l < 96 && slotLink (corner o) (slotOf (corner o) l) == l)) &&
    allBelow 216 (fun q => patchPlaq (corner o) q < 1536 &&
      patchOf (corner o) (patchPlaq (corner o) q) == q) &&
    allBelow 96 (fun s => (plaqsOf (slotLink (corner o) s)).all fun p =>
      patchOf (corner o) p < 216 && patchPlaq (corner o) (patchOf (corner o) p) == p)

end Geometry


/-! ## 3. The box constant `κ`

For a box `b`, `κ_b = 1 / λ_min(dᵀd | F_b⁽⁰⁾)`. The certificate works in the `96` slot coordinates
of a class box: a spanning matrix `Z = [I; C; 0]` (free slots, pivot slots, tree slots), a spanning
certificate `W` (pin multipliers with `W P = dW [−C | I]`), and a packed LDLᵀ certificate for
`σ (3321 Zᵀ dᵀ d Z − 500 Zᵀ Z)`. -/

section Reduction

theorem sum_range_eq_of_inj {N M : ℕ} (g h : ℕ → ℕ) (P : ℕ → Bool) (F : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hg : ∀ s < M, g s < N ∧ h (g s) = s)
    (hh : ∀ n < N, P n = true → h n < M ∧ g (h n) = n)
    (hF : ∀ n < N, P n = false → F n = 0) :
    ∑ n ∈ range N, F n = ∑ s ∈ range M, F (g s) := by
  rw [← Finset.sum_image (s := range M) (g := g) (f := F) (fun a ha b hb hab => by
    have h1 := (hg a (mem_range.mp ha)).2
    have h2 := (hg b (mem_range.mp hb)).2
    rw [← h1, ← h2, hab])]
  symm
  refine Finset.sum_subset ?_ ?_
  · intro n hn
    obtain ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩ := mem_image.mp hn
    exact mem_range.mpr (hg s (mem_range.mp hs)).1
  · intro n hn hni
    have hn' := mem_range.mp hn
    cases hP : P n
    · exact hF n hn' hP
    · exfalso; apply hni
      obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := hh n hn' hP
      exact mem_image.mpr ⟨h n, mem_range.mpr h1, h2⟩

theorem sum_fin_eq_range {N : ℕ} (f : Fin N → ℝ) (F : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hF : ∀ n (h : n < N), F n = f ⟨n, h⟩) : ∑ i, f i = ∑ n ∈ range N, F n := by
  rw [Finset.sum_range]
  exact sum_congr rfl fun i _ => (hF i i.2).symm

theorem fl_val {n : ℕ} (h : n < 1024) : fl n = ⟨n, h⟩ := Fin.ext (Nat.mod_eq_of_lt h)

theorem fl_fin (l : Fin 1024) : fl l = l := Fin.ext (Nat.mod_eq_of_lt l.2)

/-- The position of `s` in a list. -/
def pos (s : ℕ) : List ℕ → Option ℕ
  | [] => none
  | a :: as => if a = s then some 0 else (pos s as).map (· + 1)

theorem pos_spec {s : ℕ} : ∀ {L : List ℕ} {j : ℕ}, pos s L = some j →
    j < L.length ∧ L.getD j 0 = s
  | [], j, h => by simp [pos] at h
  | a :: as, j, h => by
    unfold pos at h
    by_cases ha : a = s
    · rw [if_pos ha] at h; cases h; simp [ha]
    · rw [if_neg ha] at h
      cases hp : pos s as with
      | none => rw [hp] at h; simp at h
      | some j' =>
        rw [hp] at h; simp only [Option.map_some, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h
        obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := pos_spec hp
        exact ⟨by simp; omega, by rw [List.getD_cons_succ]; exact h2⟩

theorem pos_of_mem {s : ℕ} : ∀ {L : List ℕ}, s ∈ L → ∃ j, pos s L = some j
  | [], h => absurd h (List.not_mem_nil)
  | a :: as, h => by
    unfold pos
    by_cases ha : a = s
    · exact ⟨0, by rw [if_pos ha]⟩
    · rw [if_neg ha]
      have : s ∈ as := by
        rcases List.mem_cons.mp h with h | h
        · exact absurd h.symm ha
        · exact h
      obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := pos_of_mem this
      exact ⟨j + 1, by rw [hj]; rfl⟩

/-- `∑_{i<n} f i` in kernel form. -/
def sumRange (n : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℤ) : ℤ :=
  Nat.rec (motive := fun _ => ℤ) 0 (fun i acc => Int.add acc (f i)) n

theorem sumRange_eq (n : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℤ) : sumRange n f = ∑ i ∈ range n, f i := by
  induction n with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ n ih => rw [sum_range_succ, ← ih]; rfl

/-- `∑ₑ cₑ f(sₑ)` over a list of (index, coefficient) pairs, in kernel form. -/
def lcz (f : ℕ → ℤ) : List (ℕ × ℤ) → ℤ
  | [] => 0
  | e :: es => Int.add (Int.mul e.2 (f e.1)) (lcz f es)

theorem lcz_eq (f : ℕ → ℤ) : ∀ L : List (ℕ × ℤ), lcz f L = (L.map fun e => e.2 * f e.1).sum
  | [] => rfl
  | e :: es => by rw [lcz, List.map_cons, List.sum_cons, ← lcz_eq f es]; rfl

theorem pk_lc (K n : ℕ) (u : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ) : ∀ L : List (ℕ × ℤ),
    pk K n (fun j => (L.map fun e => e.2 * u e.1 j).sum) = (L.map fun e => e.2 * pk K n (u e.1)).sum
  | [] => by simp [pk]
  | e :: es => by
    simp only [List.map_cons, List.sum_cons]
    rw [pk_add, pk_smul, pk_lc K n u es]

theorem lcz_congr {f g : ℕ → ℤ} {L : List (ℕ × ℤ)} (h : ∀ e ∈ L, e.2 = 0 ∨ f e.1 = g e.1) :
    lcz f L = lcz g L := by
  rw [lcz_eq, lcz_eq]
  congr 1
  refine List.map_congr_left fun e he => ?_
  rcases h e he with h | h <;> simp [h]

/-- A signed data row entry in kernel form. -/
def kent (w P j : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  Int.sub (Int.ofNat (Nat.mod (Nat.shiftRight P (Nat.mul w j)) (Nat.pow 2 w)))
    (Int.ofNat (Nat.pow 2 (Nat.sub w 1)))

theorem kent_eq (w P j : ℕ) : kent w P j = ent w P j := by
  show ((((P >>> (w * j)) % 2 ^ w : ℕ)) : ℤ) - ((2 ^ (w - 1) : ℕ) : ℤ) = _
  rw [ent]; push_cast; rfl

theorem shift_one_eq (K j : ℕ) : Int.ofNat (Nat.shiftLeft 1 (Nat.mul K j)) = (2 : ℤ) ^ (K * j) := by
  show ((1 <<< (K * j) : ℕ) : ℤ) = _
  rw [Nat.shiftLeft_eq, one_mul]; push_cast; rfl

theorem pk_single (K n j : ℕ) (hj : j < n) :
    pk K n (fun j' => if j = j' then 1 else 0) = 2 ^ (K * j) := by
  rw [pk]
  simp only [ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul]
  rw [sum_ite_eq]; simp [hj]

end Reduction

section KappaCert

/-- **A κ certificate** for one class box. -/
structure KCert where
  /-- the slots of the free coordinates -/
  free : List ℕ
  /-- the slots of the pivot coordinates -/
  piv : List ℕ
  /-- the width of the pivot rows -/
  wC : ℕ
  /-- the pivot rows: the value at a pivot slot is `∑ⱼ C i j · (value at free slot j)` -/
  C : List ℕ
  /-- for each pivot, the pin multipliers `(row, coefficient)` -/
  W : List (List (ℕ × ℤ))
  /-- the scale of the spanning certificate -/
  dW : ℕ
  /-- the packing width of the spanning check -/
  K2 : ℕ
  /-- the packing width of the PSD check -/
  K : ℕ
  /-- the exponent of the scale `σ = 2^sig` of the LDLᵀ certificate -/
  sig : ℕ
  /-- the width of the LDLᵀ rows -/
  wM : ℕ
  /-- the LDLᵀ rows -/
  M : List ℕ
  /-- the width of the LDLᵀ weights -/
  wd : ℕ
  /-- the LDLᵀ weights (unsigned) -/
  d : ℕ

namespace KCert

variable (c : KCert)

/-- The fibre parametrisation in slot coordinates: `Z s j` (its columns span the fibre). -/
def Z (s j : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  match pos s c.free with
  | some j' => if j' = j then 1 else 0
  | none => match pos s c.piv with
    | some i => ent c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) j
    | none => 0

/-- Row `s` of `Z`, packed in base `2^K'` (kernel form). -/
def zp (K' s : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  match pos s c.free with
  | some j' => Int.ofNat (Nat.shiftLeft 1 (Nat.mul K' j'))
  | none => match pos s c.piv with
    | some i => prow c.wC K' c.free.length (c.C.getD i 0)
    | none => 0

theorem zp_eq (K' s : ℕ) : c.zp K' s = pk K' c.free.length (c.Z s) := by
  unfold zp Z
  cases hf : pos s c.free with
  | some j' =>
    simp only
    rw [shift_one_eq, pk_single _ _ _ (pos_spec hf).1]
  | none =>
    simp only
    cases hp : pos s c.piv with
    | some i => simp only; rw [prow_eq]
    | none => simp [pk]

theorem abs_Z_le (hw : 1 ≤ c.wC) (s j : ℕ) : |c.Z s j| ≤ 2 ^ (c.wC - 1) := by
  have h1 : (1 : ℤ) ≤ 2 ^ (c.wC - 1) := one_le_pow₀ (by norm_num)
  unfold Z
  cases hf : pos s c.free with
  | some j' => simp only; split_ifs <;> simp [h1]
  | none =>
    simp only
    cases hp : pos s c.piv with
    | some i => exact abs_ent_le hw _ _
    | none => simp

end KCert

/-- The four `(slot, coefficient)` entries of the local plaquette operator at the patch slot
`q` of the box with corner `b` (coefficient `0` for a link not touching the box). -/
def dlocOf (b q : ℕ) : List (ℕ × ℤ) :=
  (List.range 4).map fun i => (slotOf b (plaqLink (patchPlaq b q) i % 1024),
    if touches b (plaqLink (patchPlaq b q) i % 1024) then (if i < 2 then 1 else -1) else 0)

theorem dlocOf_coef (b q : ℕ) : ∀ e ∈ dlocOf b q, |e.2| ≤ 1 := by
  intro e he
  simp only [dlocOf, List.mem_map, List.mem_range] at he
  obtain ⟨i, _, rfl⟩ := he
  split_ifs <;> simp

theorem dlocOf_length (b q : ℕ) : (dlocOf b q).length = 4 := by simp [dlocOf]

namespace KCert

variable (c : KCert)

/-- The curvature of the columns of `Z` at the patch slot `q`: `K q j = ∑ₑ cₑ Z sₑ j`. -/
def Kq (b q j : ℕ) : ℤ := ((dlocOf b q).map fun e => e.2 * c.Z e.1 j).sum

/-- The form `σ (3321 Kᵀ K − 500 Zᵀ Z)`, whose positivity is the bound `κ ≤ 3321/500`. -/
def H (b i j : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  2 ^ c.sig * (3321 * ∑ q ∈ range 216, c.Kq b q i * c.Kq b q j -
    500 * ∑ s ∈ range 96, c.Z s i * c.Z s j)

/-- The entry bound used for `H`. -/
def βH : ℕ :=
  2 ^ c.sig * (3321 * 216 * (4 * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1)) * (4 * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1)) +
    500 * 96 * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1) * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1))

/-- `H`, packed with index `i + k j` (kernel form). -/
def Hpk (b : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  let k := c.free.length
  let zx := (List.range 96).map (c.zp c.K)
  let zy := (List.range 96).map (c.zp (Nat.mul c.K k))
  Int.mul (Int.ofNat (Nat.pow 2 c.sig))
    (Int.sub (Int.mul 3321 (sumRange 216 fun q => Int.mul (lcz (fun s => zx.getD s 0) (dlocOf b q))
        (lcz (fun s => zy.getD s 0) (dlocOf b q))))
      (Int.mul 500 (sumRange 96 fun s => Int.mul (zx.getD s 0) (zy.getD s 0))))

theorem getD_map_range (f : ℕ → ℤ) {s n : ℕ} (hs : s < n) :
    ((List.range n).map f).getD s 0 = f s := by
  rw [List.getD_eq_getElem?_getD, List.getElem?_map, List.getElem?_range hs]; rfl

theorem abs_Kq_le (hw : 1 ≤ c.wC) (b q j : ℕ) : |c.Kq b q j| ≤ 4 * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1) := by
  unfold Kq
  have : ∀ L : List (ℕ × ℤ), (∀ e ∈ L, |e.2| ≤ 1) →
      |(L.map fun e => e.2 * c.Z e.1 j).sum| ≤ L.length * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1) := by
    intro L
    induction L with
    | nil => simp
    | cons e es ih =>
      intro hL
      simp only [List.map_cons, List.sum_cons, List.length_cons]
      have h1 := hL e (List.mem_cons_self ..)
      have h2 := ih fun e' he' => hL e' (List.mem_cons_of_mem _ he')
      have h3 := c.abs_Z_le hw e.1 j
      calc |e.2 * c.Z e.1 j + (es.map fun e => e.2 * c.Z e.1 j).sum|
          ≤ |e.2 * c.Z e.1 j| + |(es.map fun e => e.2 * c.Z e.1 j).sum| := abs_add_le _ _
        _ ≤ 1 * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1) + es.length * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1) := by
          rw [abs_mul]
          exact add_le_add (mul_le_mul h1 h3 (abs_nonneg _) zero_le_one) h2
        _ = _ := by push_cast; ring
  have := this _ (dlocOf_coef b q)
  rwa [dlocOf_length] at this

theorem abs_H_le (hw : 1 ≤ c.wC) (b i j : ℕ) : |c.H b i j| ≤ c.βH := by
  unfold H βH
  set z : ℤ := 2 ^ (c.wC - 1)
  have hz : 0 ≤ z := by positivity
  have hG : |∑ q ∈ range 216, c.Kq b q i * c.Kq b q j| ≤ 216 * (4 * z) * (4 * z) := by
    refine (abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans ?_
    have : ∀ q ∈ range 216, |c.Kq b q i * c.Kq b q j| ≤ (4 * z) * (4 * z) := fun q _ => by
      rw [abs_mul]; exact mul_le_mul (c.abs_Kq_le hw _ _ _) (c.abs_Kq_le hw _ _ _)
        (abs_nonneg _) (by positivity)
    refine (sum_le_sum this).trans ?_
    rw [sum_const, card_range, nsmul_eq_mul]; push_cast; ring_nf; exact le_refl _
  have hN : |∑ s ∈ range 96, c.Z s i * c.Z s j| ≤ 96 * z * z := by
    refine (abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans ?_
    have : ∀ s ∈ range 96, |c.Z s i * c.Z s j| ≤ z * z := fun s _ => by
      rw [abs_mul]; exact mul_le_mul (c.abs_Z_le hw _ _) (c.abs_Z_le hw _ _)
        (abs_nonneg _) hz
    refine (sum_le_sum this).trans ?_
    rw [sum_const, card_range, nsmul_eq_mul]; push_cast; ring_nf; exact le_refl _
  have hs : (0 : ℤ) ≤ 2 ^ c.sig := by positivity
  rw [abs_mul, abs_of_nonneg hs]
  push_cast
  refine mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ?_ hs
  refine (abs_sub _ _).trans ?_
  rw [abs_mul, abs_mul]
  have e1 : |(3321 : ℤ)| = 3321 := by norm_num
  have e2 : |(500 : ℤ)| = 500 := by norm_num
  rw [e1, e2]
  nlinarith [hG, hN]

theorem H_symm (b i j : ℕ) : c.H b i j = c.H b j i := by
  unfold H
  congr 2
  · congr 1; exact sum_congr rfl fun q _ => mul_comm _ _
  · congr 1; exact sum_congr rfl fun s _ => mul_comm _ _

end KCert

end KappaCert


section KappaSound

theorem site4_lt (a b c d : ℕ) : site4 a b c d < 256 := by unfold site4; omega

theorem coord_lt (s a : ℕ) : coord s a < 4 := by unfold coord; exact Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num)

theorem planeMu_lt (k : ℕ) : planeMu k < 4 := by
  unfold planeMu
  rcases k with _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | k <;> simp

theorem planeNu_lt (k : ℕ) : planeNu k < 4 := by
  unfold planeNu
  rcases k with _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | k <;> simp

theorem natpow_eq (m n : ℕ) : Nat.pow m n = m ^ n := rfl

theorem geom_facts (hg : geomCheck = true) :
    (∀ t < 16, ∀ s < 256, trSite t (trSite t s) = s ∧ trSite t s < 256 ∧
      ∀ a < 4, step (trSite t s) a = trSite t (step s a) ∧
        coord (trSite t s) a = (coord s a + 2 * bit t a) % 4) ∧
    (∀ t < 16, ∀ l < 1024, isTree (trL t l) = isTree l) ∧
    (∀ t < 16, ∀ Z < 16, ∀ o < 16, trSite t (blockSite Z o) = blockSite (Z ^^^ t) o) ∧
    (∀ b < 256, trSite (trOf b) (corner (clsOf b)) = b ∧ clsOf b < 16 ∧ trOf b < 16) ∧
    (∀ s < 256, ∀ a < 4, step s a < 256) ∧
    (∀ p < 1536, ∀ i < 4, p ∈ plaqsOf (plaqLink p i) ∧ plaqLink p i < 1024) := by
  unfold geomCheck at hg
  simp only [Bool.and_eq_true, allBelow_iff, beq_iff_eq, decide_eq_true_eq,
    List.contains_iff_mem] at hg
  obtain ⟨⟨⟨⟨⟨h1, h2⟩, h3⟩, h4⟩, h5⟩, h6⟩ := hg
  exact ⟨fun t ht s hs => ⟨(h1 t ht s hs).1.1, (h1 t ht s hs).1.2, (h1 t ht s hs).2⟩, h2, h3,
    fun b hb => ⟨(h4 b hb).1.1, (h4 b hb).1.2, (h4 b hb).2⟩, h5, h6⟩

theorem slot_facts (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) :
    (∀ s < 96, slotLink (corner o) s < 1024 ∧ touches (corner o) (slotLink (corner o) s) = true ∧
      slotOf (corner o) (slotLink (corner o) s) = s) ∧
    (∀ l < 1024, touches (corner o) l = true →
      slotOf (corner o) l < 96 ∧ slotLink (corner o) (slotOf (corner o) l) = l) ∧
    (∀ q < 216, patchPlaq (corner o) q < 1536 ∧ patchOf (corner o) (patchPlaq (corner o) q) = q) ∧
    (∀ s < 96, ∀ p ∈ plaqsOf (slotLink (corner o) s),
      patchOf (corner o) p < 216 ∧ patchPlaq (corner o) (patchOf (corner o) p) = p) := by
  have h := (allBelow_iff.mp hs) o ho
  simp only [Bool.and_eq_true, allBelow_iff, beq_iff_eq, decide_eq_true_eq, Bool.or_eq_true,
    Bool.not_eq_true', List.all_eq_true] at h
  obtain ⟨⟨⟨h1, h2⟩, h3⟩, h4⟩ := h
  refine ⟨fun s hs => ⟨(h1 s hs).1.1, (h1 s hs).1.2, (h1 s hs).2⟩, fun l hl ht => ?_, h3, h4⟩
  rcases h2 l hl with h | h
  · rw [ht] at h; exact absurd h (by decide)
  · exact h

/-- Values of a fibre field through the slots: a touching link is the link of its slot. -/
theorem phi_touch (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ} (n : ℕ)
    (hn : touches (corner o) (n % 1024) = true) :
    φ (fl n) = φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) (slotOf (corner o) (n % 1024)))) := by
  have := ((slot_facts hs ho).2.1 (n % 1024) (Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num)) hn).2
  rw [this]
  exact congrArg φ (Fin.ext (by simp [fl]))

theorem phi_untouch {o : ℕ} {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ} (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (corner o)) (n : ℕ)
    (hn : touches (corner o) (n % 1024) = false) : φ (fl n) = 0 :=
  hφ.2 (fl n) hn

/-- The packed slot vector of a pin term `n`: `2^(K₂ s)` if `n` is a non-tree link touching the
box at the slot `s`, and `0` otherwise (kernel form). -/
def contrib (b K2 n : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  if (touches b (n % 1024) && !isTree (n % 1024)) = true then
    Int.ofNat (Nat.shiftLeft 1 (Nat.mul K2 (slotOf b (n % 1024)))) else 0

/-- The slot indicator of a pin term. -/
def cnt (b n s : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  if (touches b (n % 1024) && !isTree (n % 1024)) = true ∧ slotOf b (n % 1024) = s then 1 else 0

/-- The slot coefficients of the pin row `r` (non-tree links touching the box). -/
def pinA (b r s : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  ∑ o ∈ range 16, (cnt b (4 * blockSite (r % 16) o + r / 16) s +
    cnt b (4 * step (blockSite (r % 16) o) (r / 16) + r / 16) s)

/-- The pin row `r` packed over the slots (kernel form). -/
def pinPack (b K2 r : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  sumRange 16 fun o => Int.add (contrib b K2 (4 * blockSite (r % 16) o + r / 16))
    (contrib b K2 (4 * step (blockSite (r % 16) o) (r / 16) + r / 16))

theorem contrib_eq (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) (K2 n : ℕ) :
    contrib (corner o) K2 n = pk K2 96 (cnt (corner o) n) := by
  unfold contrib cnt
  by_cases h : (touches (corner o) (n % 1024) && !isTree (n % 1024)) = true
  · rw [if_pos h, shift_one_eq]
    have hlt : slotOf (corner o) (n % 1024) < 96 := by
      have ht : touches (corner o) (n % 1024) = true := by
        simp only [Bool.and_eq_true] at h; exact h.1
      exact ((slot_facts hs ho).2.1 _ (Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num)) ht).1
    have : (fun s => if (touches (corner o) (n % 1024) && !isTree (n % 1024)) = true ∧
        slotOf (corner o) (n % 1024) = s then (1 : ℤ) else 0) =
        fun s => if slotOf (corner o) (n % 1024) = s then 1 else 0 := by
      funext s; simp only [h, true_and]
    rw [this, pk_single _ _ _ hlt]
  · rw [if_neg h]
    simp [pk, h]

theorem pinPack_eq (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) (K2 r : ℕ) :
    pinPack (corner o) K2 r = pk K2 96 (pinA (corner o) r) := by
  unfold pinPack pinA
  rw [sumRange_eq, pk_sum]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [pk_add, ← contrib_eq hs ho, ← contrib_eq hs ho]; rfl

/-- A fibre field at a pin term, as a combination of its slot values. -/
theorem phi_cnt (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ}
    (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (corner o)) (n : ℕ) :
    φ (fl n) = ∑ s ∈ range 96, (cnt (corner o) n s : ℝ) * φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) := by
  unfold cnt
  by_cases ht : touches (corner o) (n % 1024) = true
  · have hlt := ((slot_facts hs ho).2.1 _ (Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num)) ht).1
    by_cases htr : isTree (n % 1024) = true
    · have h0 : φ (fl n) = 0 := hφ.1.1 (fl n) (by simpa [fl] using htr)
      rw [h0]; symm; refine sum_eq_zero fun s _ => ?_
      simp [htr]
    · have hok : (touches (corner o) (n % 1024) && !isTree (n % 1024)) = true := by
        simp [ht, htr]
      simp only [hok, true_and]
      push_cast
      simp only [ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul]
      rw [sum_ite_eq, if_pos (mem_range.mpr hlt)]
      exact phi_touch hs ho n ht
  · rw [Bool.not_eq_true] at ht
    rw [phi_untouch hφ n ht]; symm; refine sum_eq_zero fun s _ => ?_
    simp [ht]

theorem pinSum_slots (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ}
    (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (corner o)) (r : ℕ) (hr : r < 64) :
    pinSum ⟨r, hr⟩ φ =
      ∑ s ∈ range 96, (pinA (corner o) r s : ℝ) * φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) := by
  unfold pinSum pinA
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_eq_sum_range (fun i => φ (fl (4 * blockSite (r % 16) i + r / 16)) +
    φ (fl (4 * step (blockSite (r % 16) i) (r / 16) + r / 16))) 16]
  have e : ∀ i ∈ range 16, φ (fl (4 * blockSite (r % 16) i + r / 16)) +
      φ (fl (4 * step (blockSite (r % 16) i) (r / 16) + r / 16)) =
      ∑ s ∈ range 96, ((cnt (corner o) (4 * blockSite (r % 16) i + r / 16) s : ℝ) +
        (cnt (corner o) (4 * step (blockSite (r % 16) i) (r / 16) + r / 16) s : ℝ)) *
          φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) := by
    intro i _
    rw [phi_cnt hs ho hφ (4 * blockSite (r % 16) i + r / 16),
      phi_cnt hs ho hφ (4 * step (blockSite (r % 16) i) (r / 16) + r / 16), ← sum_add_distrib]
    exact sum_congr rfl fun s _ => by ring
  rw [sum_congr rfl e, sum_comm]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun s _ => ?_
  rw [← sum_mul]
  push_cast
  rfl

/-- The spanning row of the pivot `i`: `dW (e_{piv i} − ∑ⱼ C i j e_{free j})`. -/
def spanRow (c : KCert) (i s : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  c.dW * ((if c.piv.getD i 0 = s then 1 else 0) -
    ∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, ent c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) j * (if c.free.getD j 0 = s then 1 else 0))

/-- `∑ⱼ (C i j) 2^(K₂ free j)` (kernel form), from the index `j`. -/
def freeComb (w P K2 : ℕ) : List ℕ → ℕ → ℤ
  | [], _ => 0
  | f :: fs, j => Int.add (Int.mul (kent w P j) (Int.ofNat (Nat.shiftLeft 1 (Nat.mul K2 f))))
      (freeComb w P K2 fs (j + 1))

theorem freeComb_eq (w P K2 : ℕ) : ∀ (L : List ℕ) (j0 : ℕ), (∀ f ∈ L, f < 96) →
    freeComb w P K2 L j0 = pk K2 96 (fun s => ∑ j ∈ range L.length,
      ent w P (j0 + j) * (if L.getD j 0 = s then 1 else 0))
  | [], j0, _ => by simp [freeComb, pk]
  | f :: fs, j0, hL => by
    show kent w P j0 * Int.ofNat (Nat.shiftLeft 1 (Nat.mul K2 f)) + freeComb w P K2 fs (j0 + 1) = _
    rw [freeComb_eq w P K2 fs (j0 + 1) (fun f' hf' => hL f' (List.mem_cons_of_mem _ hf')),
      kent_eq, shift_one_eq, ← pk_single K2 96 f (hL f (List.mem_cons_self ..)), ← pk_smul,
      ← pk_add]
    refine pk_congr fun s _ => ?_
    rw [List.length_cons, sum_range_succ']
    simp only [List.getD_cons_zero, List.getD_cons_succ, add_zero]
    rw [add_comm]
    congr 1
    refine sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
    rw [show j0 + 1 + j = j0 + (j + 1) by ring]

/-- The spanning row packed over the slots (kernel form). -/
def rowPack (c : KCert) (i : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  Int.mul (Int.ofNat c.dW) (Int.sub (Int.ofNat (Nat.shiftLeft 1 (Nat.mul c.K2 (c.piv.getD i 0))))
    (freeComb c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) c.K2 c.free 0))

theorem rowPack_eq (c : KCert) (i : ℕ) (hp : c.piv.getD i 0 < 96) (hf : ∀ f ∈ c.free, f < 96) :
    rowPack c i = pk c.K2 96 (spanRow c i) := by
  show (c.dW : ℤ) * (Int.ofNat (Nat.shiftLeft 1 (Nat.mul c.K2 (c.piv.getD i 0))) -
    freeComb c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) c.K2 c.free 0) = _
  rw [shift_one_eq, freeComb_eq _ _ _ _ _ hf, ← pk_single c.K2 96 _ hp, ← pk_sub, ← pk_smul]
  refine pk_congr fun s _ => ?_
  simp only [spanRow, zero_add]

/-- The total absolute weight of a list of multipliers. -/
def wsum (L : List (ℕ × ℤ)) : ℕ := (L.map fun e => e.2.natAbs).sum

theorem wsum_cons (e : ℕ × ℤ) (L : List (ℕ × ℤ)) : wsum (e :: L) = e.2.natAbs + wsum L := by
  simp [wsum]

/-- **The spanning check** for the pivot `i` (kernel form). -/
def spanOK (b : ℕ) (c : KCert) (i : ℕ) : Bool :=
  (c.W.getD i []).all (fun e => decide (e.1 < 64)) &&
  decide (32 * wsum (c.W.getD i []) + c.dW * (1 + c.free.length * Nat.pow 2 (c.wC - 1)) <
    Nat.pow 2 c.K2) &&
  decide (lcz (pinPack b c.K2) (c.W.getD i []) = rowPack c i)

/-- The kernel form of `βH`. -/
def KCert.βHk (c : KCert) : ℕ :=
  Nat.pow 2 c.sig * (3321 * 216 * (4 * Nat.pow 2 (c.wC - 1)) * (4 * Nat.pow 2 (c.wC - 1)) +
    500 * 96 * Nat.pow 2 (c.wC - 1) * Nat.pow 2 (c.wC - 1))

theorem KCert.βHk_eq (c : KCert) : c.βHk = c.βH := rfl

/-- Every slot is a free slot, a pivot slot, or a tree slot. -/
def kRoles (o : ℕ) (c : KCert) : Bool :=
  allBelow 96 fun s => c.free.contains s || c.piv.contains s || isTree (slotLink (corner o) s)

/-- Ranges and positivity of the parameters. -/
def kRanges (c : KCert) : Bool :=
  c.free.all (fun s => decide (s < 96)) && c.piv.all (fun s => decide (s < 96)) &&
  decide (0 < c.dW) && decide (1 ≤ c.wC) && decide (1 ≤ c.wM) && decide (1 ≤ c.K)

/-- The spanning checks of all pivots. -/
def kSpan (o : ℕ) (c : KCert) : Bool := allBelow c.piv.length (spanOK (corner o) c)

/-- The size condition of the packed PSD check. -/
def kBound (c : KCert) : Bool :=
  decide (2 * (c.βHk + c.M.length * Nat.pow 2 c.wd * Nat.pow 2 (c.wM - 1) * Nat.pow 2 (c.wM - 1))
    < Nat.pow 2 c.K)

/-- The packed PSD check. -/
def kPsd (o : ℕ) (c : KCert) : Bool :=
  psdScan c.K c.free.length c.free.length 0
    (Int.sub (c.Hpk (corner o)) (ldlSum c.K c.free.length c.wM c.wd c.d c.M 0))

/-- **Validity of a κ certificate** for the class box `o` (a closed Boolean computation). -/
def kappaCheck (o : ℕ) (c : KCert) : Bool :=
  kRoles o c && kRanges c && kSpan o c && kBound c && kPsd o c

theorem kappaCheck_parts {o : ℕ} {c : KCert} (h : kappaCheck o c = true) :
    kRoles o c = true ∧ kRanges c = true ∧ kSpan o c = true ∧ kBound c = true ∧
      kPsd o c = true := by
  unfold kappaCheck at h
  rw [Bool.and_eq_true, Bool.and_eq_true, Bool.and_eq_true, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
  exact ⟨h.1.1.1.1, h.1.1.1.2, h.1.1.2, h.1.2, h.2⟩

theorem kRanges_parts {c : KCert} (h : kRanges c = true) :
    (∀ s ∈ c.free, s < 96) ∧ (∀ s ∈ c.piv, s < 96) ∧ 0 < c.dW ∧ 1 ≤ c.wC ∧ 1 ≤ c.wM ∧
      1 ≤ c.K := by
  unfold kRanges at h
  simp only [Bool.and_eq_true, decide_eq_true_eq, List.all_eq_true] at h
  exact ⟨h.1.1.1.1.1, h.1.1.1.1.2, h.1.1.1.2, h.1.1.2, h.1.2, h.2⟩

theorem pinA_bound (b r s : ℕ) : |pinA b r s| ≤ 32 := by
  unfold pinA
  refine (abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans ?_
  have : ∀ o ∈ range 16, |cnt b (4 * blockSite (r % 16) o + r / 16) s +
      cnt b (4 * step (blockSite (r % 16) o) (r / 16) + r / 16) s| ≤ 2 := by
    intro o _
    refine (abs_add_le _ _).trans ?_
    unfold cnt
    split_ifs <;> norm_num
  refine (sum_le_sum this).trans ?_
  simp

theorem lc_bound (L : List (ℕ × ℤ)) (f : ℕ → ℤ) (B : ℤ) (hB : ∀ n, |f n| ≤ B) :
    |(L.map fun e => e.2 * f e.1).sum| ≤ (wsum L : ℤ) * B := by
  induction L with
  | nil => simp [wsum]
  | cons e es ih =>
    rw [List.map_cons, List.sum_cons, wsum_cons]
    have h1 : |e.2 * f e.1| ≤ (e.2.natAbs : ℤ) * B := by
      rw [abs_mul, Int.abs_eq_natAbs e.2]
      exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hB e.1) (Int.natCast_nonneg e.2.natAbs)
    have h2 := abs_add_le (e.2 * f e.1) (es.map fun e => e.2 * f e.1).sum
    rw [Nat.cast_add, add_mul]
    linarith

theorem abs_spanRow_le (c : KCert) (i s : ℕ) (hw : 1 ≤ c.wC) :
    |spanRow c i s| ≤ c.dW * (1 + c.free.length * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1)) := by
  unfold spanRow
  rw [abs_mul, abs_of_nonneg (Int.natCast_nonneg _)]
  refine mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ?_ (Int.natCast_nonneg _)
  refine (abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add ?_ ?_)
  · split_ifs <;> simp
  · refine (abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans ?_
    have : ∀ j ∈ range c.free.length, |ent c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) j *
        (if c.free.getD j 0 = s then 1 else 0)| ≤ 2 ^ (c.wC - 1) := by
      intro j _
      rw [abs_mul]
      have h1 := abs_ent_le hw (c.C.getD i 0) j
      have h2 : |(if c.free.getD j 0 = s then (1 : ℤ) else 0)| ≤ 1 := by split_ifs <;> simp
      nlinarith [abs_nonneg (ent c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) j)]
    refine (sum_le_sum this).trans ?_
    rw [sum_const, card_range, nsmul_eq_mul]

theorem sum_list_comm {n : ℕ} (L : List (ℕ × ℤ)) (g : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ) (v : ℕ → ℝ) :
    ∑ s ∈ range n, (((L.map fun e => e.2 * g e.1 s).sum : ℤ) : ℝ) * v s =
      (L.map fun e => (e.2 : ℝ) * ∑ s ∈ range n, (g e.1 s : ℝ) * v s).sum := by
  induction L with
  | nil => simp
  | cons e es ih =>
    simp only [List.map_cons, List.sum_cons]
    rw [← ih, mul_sum, ← sum_add_distrib]
    refine sum_congr rfl fun s _ => ?_
    push_cast
    ring

theorem spanRow_sum (c : KCert) (i : ℕ) (v : ℕ → ℝ) (hp : c.piv.getD i 0 < 96)
    (hf : ∀ j < c.free.length, c.free.getD j 0 < 96) :
    ∑ s ∈ range 96, (spanRow c i s : ℝ) * v s = c.dW * (v (c.piv.getD i 0) -
      ∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (ent c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) j : ℝ) * v (c.free.getD j 0)) := by
  have hterm : ∀ s, (spanRow c i s : ℝ) * v s = (c.dW : ℝ) *
      ((if c.piv.getD i 0 = s then v s else 0) - ∑ j ∈ range c.free.length,
        (ent c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) j : ℝ) * (if c.free.getD j 0 = s then v s else 0)) := by
    intro s
    unfold spanRow
    push_cast
    rw [mul_assoc, sub_mul, sum_mul]
    congr 2
    · split_ifs <;> simp
    · exact sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by split_ifs <;> simp
  rw [sum_congr rfl fun s _ => hterm s, ← mul_sum, sum_sub_distrib, sum_ite_eq,
    if_pos (mem_range.mpr hp), sum_comm]
  congr 2
  refine sum_congr rfl fun j hj => ?_
  rw [← mul_sum, sum_ite_eq, if_pos (mem_range.mpr (hf j (mem_range.mp hj)))]

/-- The slot coefficients of a combination of pins. -/
def spanA (o : ℕ) (L : List (ℕ × ℤ)) (s : ℕ) : ℤ := (L.map fun e => e.2 * pinA (corner o) e.1 s).sum

theorem spanA_pk (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) (K2 : ℕ) (L : List (ℕ × ℤ)) :
    lcz (pinPack (corner o) K2) L = pk K2 96 (spanA o L) := by
  unfold spanA
  rw [lcz_eq, pk_lc]
  refine congrArg List.sum (List.map_congr_left fun e _ => ?_)
  rw [pinPack_eq hs ho]

theorem spanA_bound (o : ℕ) (L : List (ℕ × ℤ)) (s : ℕ) : |spanA o L s| ≤ (wsum L : ℤ) * 32 :=
  lc_bound L (fun n => pinA (corner o) n s) 32 fun _ => pinA_bound _ _ _

theorem spanA_sum (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ}
    (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (corner o)) (L : List (ℕ × ℤ)) (hL : ∀ e ∈ L, e.1 < 64) :
    ∑ s ∈ range 96, (spanA o L s : ℝ) * φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) = 0 := by
  unfold spanA
  rw [sum_list_comm]
  refine List.sum_eq_zero fun x hx => ?_
  obtain ⟨e, he, rfl⟩ := List.mem_map.mp hx
  rw [← pinSum_slots hs ho hφ e.1 (hL e he), hφ.1.2 ⟨e.1, hL e he⟩, mul_zero]

/-- **Spanning.** If the check succeeds, every pivot value of a fibre field is the combination
`∑ⱼ C i j · (value at free slot j)`. -/
theorem pivot_value (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) {c : KCert}
    (hc : kappaCheck o c = true) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ} (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (corner o)) {i : ℕ}
    (hi : i < c.piv.length) :
    φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) (c.piv.getD i 0))) = ∑ j ∈ range c.free.length,
      (ent c.wC (c.C.getD i 0) j : ℝ) * φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) (c.free.getD j 0))) := by
  obtain ⟨_, hR, hspan, _, _⟩ := kappaCheck_parts hc
  obtain ⟨hfree, hpiv, hdW, hwC, _, _⟩ := kRanges_parts hR
  have hsp := (allBelow_iff.mp hspan) i hi
  unfold spanOK at hsp
  rw [Bool.and_eq_true, Bool.and_eq_true, decide_eq_true_eq, decide_eq_true_eq,
    List.all_eq_true] at hsp
  obtain ⟨⟨hr64, hbig⟩, heq⟩ := hsp
  have hL : ∀ e ∈ c.W.getD i [], e.1 < 64 := fun e he => of_decide_eq_true (hr64 e he)
  have hp96 : c.piv.getD i 0 < 96 := hpiv _ (by
    rw [List.getD_eq_getElem?_getD, List.getElem?_eq_getElem hi]; exact List.getElem_mem hi)
  have hpk : pk c.K2 96 (spanA o (c.W.getD i [])) = pk c.K2 96 (spanRow c i) := by
    rw [← spanA_pk hs ho, heq, rowPack_eq c i hp96 hfree]
  rw [natpow_eq, natpow_eq] at hbig
  have hbig' : ((32 * wsum (c.W.getD i []) + c.dW * (1 + c.free.length * 2 ^ (c.wC - 1)) : ℕ) : ℤ)
      < ((2 ^ c.K2 : ℕ) : ℤ) := by exact_mod_cast hbig
  push_cast at hbig'
  have hAR : ∀ s < 96, spanA o (c.W.getD i []) s = spanRow c i s := by
    have h0 : pk c.K2 96 (fun s => spanA o (c.W.getD i []) s - spanRow c i s) = 0 := by
      rw [pk_sub, hpk, sub_self]
    have hb : ∀ s < 96, |spanA o (c.W.getD i []) s - spanRow c i s| < 2 ^ c.K2 := by
      intro s _
      have h1 := spanA_bound o (c.W.getD i []) s
      have h2 := abs_spanRow_le c i s hwC
      calc |spanA o (c.W.getD i []) s - spanRow c i s|
          ≤ |spanA o (c.W.getD i []) s| + |spanRow c i s| := abs_sub _ _
        _ < 2 ^ c.K2 := by linarith
    intro s hs'
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp (eq_zero_of_pk hb h0 s hs')
  have h3 : ∑ s ∈ range 96, (spanRow c i s : ℝ) * φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) = 0 := by
    rw [← spanA_sum hs ho hφ (c.W.getD i []) hL]
    exact sum_congr rfl fun s hs' => by rw [hAR s (mem_range.mp hs')]
  have hf96 : ∀ j < c.free.length, c.free.getD j 0 < 96 := fun j hj => hfree _ (by
    rw [List.getD_eq_getElem?_getD, List.getElem?_eq_getElem hj]; exact List.getElem_mem hj)
  rw [spanRow_sum c i _ hp96 hf96] at h3
  have hdW' : (0 : ℝ) < c.dW := by exact_mod_cast hdW
  have := (mul_eq_zero.mp h3).resolve_left hdW'.ne'
  linarith

end KappaSound

section KappaClass

/-- The plaquette with index `n` (reduced modulo `1536`). -/
def flp (n : ℕ) : Fin 1536 := ⟨n % 1536, Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num)⟩

theorem flp_val {n : ℕ} (h : n < 1536) : flp n = ⟨n, h⟩ := Fin.ext (Nat.mod_eq_of_lt h)

theorem KCert.zp_getD (c : KCert) (K' s : ℕ) (hs : s < 96) :
    ((List.range 96).map (c.zp K')).getD s 0 = pk K' c.free.length (c.Z s) := by
  rw [KCert.getD_map_range _ hs, c.zp_eq]

theorem dloc_slot (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) (q : ℕ) :
    ∀ e ∈ dlocOf (corner o) q, e.2 = 0 ∨ e.1 < 96 := by
  intro e he
  simp only [dlocOf, List.mem_map, List.mem_range] at he
  obtain ⟨i, _, rfl⟩ := he
  by_cases ht : touches (corner o) (plaqLink (patchPlaq (corner o) q) i % 1024) = true
  · right; exact ((slot_facts hs ho).2.1 _ (Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num)) ht).1
  · left; simp [ht]

theorem KCert.lc_pk (c : KCert) (K' : ℕ) {L : List (ℕ × ℤ)} (hL : ∀ e ∈ L, e.2 = 0 ∨ e.1 < 96) :
    lcz (fun s => ((List.range 96).map (c.zp K')).getD s 0) L =
      pk K' c.free.length (fun j => (L.map fun e => e.2 * c.Z e.1 j).sum) := by
  rw [pk_lc, lcz_eq]
  refine congrArg List.sum (List.map_congr_left fun e he => ?_)
  rcases hL e he with h | h
  · simp [h]
  · rw [c.zp_getD K' e.1 h]

theorem pk_gram (K n m : ℕ) (u : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ) :
    pk K (n * n) (fun t => ∑ q ∈ range m, u q (t % n) * u q (t / n)) =
      ∑ q ∈ range m, pk K n (u q) * pk (K * n) n (u q) := by
  rw [pk_sum]; exact sum_congr rfl fun q _ => (pk_mul K n (u q) (u q)).symm

theorem imul_eq (a b : ℤ) : Int.mul a b = a * b := rfl
theorem iadd_eq (a b : ℤ) : Int.add a b = a + b := rfl
theorem isub_eq (a b : ℤ) : Int.sub a b = a - b := rfl

theorem KCert.Hpk_eq (c : KCert) (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) :
    c.Hpk (corner o) = pk c.K (c.free.length * c.free.length)
      (fun t => c.H (corner o) (t % c.free.length) (t / c.free.length)) := by
  have hA : ∀ q ∈ range 216,
      lcz (fun s => ((List.range 96).map (c.zp c.K)).getD s 0) (dlocOf (corner o) q) *
        lcz (fun s => ((List.range 96).map (c.zp (c.K * c.free.length))).getD s 0)
          (dlocOf (corner o) q) =
      pk c.K c.free.length (c.Kq (corner o) q) *
        pk (c.K * c.free.length) c.free.length (c.Kq (corner o) q) := fun q _ => by
    rw [c.lc_pk _ (dloc_slot hs ho q), c.lc_pk _ (dloc_slot hs ho q)]; rfl
  have hB : ∀ s ∈ range 96,
      ((List.range 96).map (c.zp c.K)).getD s 0 *
        ((List.range 96).map (c.zp (c.K * c.free.length))).getD s 0 =
      pk c.K c.free.length (c.Z s) * pk (c.K * c.free.length) c.free.length (c.Z s) :=
    fun s hs' => by rw [c.zp_getD _ s (mem_range.mp hs'), c.zp_getD _ s (mem_range.mp hs')]
  have e1 : c.Hpk (corner o) = 2 ^ c.sig * (3321 * ∑ q ∈ range 216,
      pk c.K c.free.length (c.Kq (corner o) q) * pk (c.K * c.free.length) c.free.length
        (c.Kq (corner o) q) -
      500 * ∑ s ∈ range 96, pk c.K c.free.length (c.Z s) *
        pk (c.K * c.free.length) c.free.length (c.Z s)) := by
    unfold KCert.Hpk
    simp only [sumRange_eq, imul_eq, isub_eq, Int.ofNat_eq_natCast, natpow_eq, Nat.mul_eq]
    rw [sum_congr rfl hA, sum_congr rfl hB]
    push_cast
    rfl
  rw [e1]
  symm
  show pk c.K (c.free.length * c.free.length) (fun t => 2 ^ c.sig *
    (3321 * ∑ q ∈ range 216, c.Kq (corner o) q (t % c.free.length) *
      c.Kq (corner o) q (t / c.free.length) -
    500 * ∑ s ∈ range 96, c.Z s (t % c.free.length) * c.Z s (t / c.free.length))) = _
  rw [pk_smul, pk_sub, pk_smul, pk_smul, pk_gram, pk_gram]

theorem qf_gram (n m : ℕ) (u : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) (y : ℕ → ℝ) :
    qf n (fun i j => ∑ t ∈ range m, u t i * u t j) y = ∑ t ∈ range m, (∑ i ∈ range n, u t i * y i) ^ 2 := by
  have := qf_ldl (n := n) (m := m) (H := fun i j => ∑ t ∈ range m, u t i * u t j)
    (R := fun _ _ => 0) (M := u) (d := fun _ => 1) (fun i _ j _ => by simp) y
  rw [this]
  simp [qf]

theorem qf_lin (n : ℕ) (a b1 b2 : ℝ) (A B : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) (y : ℕ → ℝ) :
    qf n (fun i j => a * (b1 * A i j - b2 * B i j)) y = a * (b1 * qf n A y - b2 * qf n B y) := by
  simp only [qf, mul_sum, ← sum_sub_distrib]
  exact sum_congr rfl fun i _ => sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by ring

theorem slot_value (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) {c : KCert}
    (hc : kappaCheck o c = true) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ} (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (corner o)) {s : ℕ}
    (hs96 : s < 96) :
    φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) = ∑ j ∈ range c.free.length,
      (c.Z s j : ℝ) * φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) (c.free.getD j 0))) := by
  obtain ⟨hroles, _, _, _, _⟩ := kappaCheck_parts hc
  unfold KCert.Z
  cases hf : pos s c.free with
  | some j' =>
    obtain ⟨hj', hget⟩ := pos_spec hf
    simp only
    push_cast
    simp only [ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul]
    rw [sum_ite_eq, if_pos (mem_range.mpr hj'), hget]
  | none =>
    cases hp : pos s c.piv with
    | some i =>
      obtain ⟨hi, hget⟩ := pos_spec hp
      simp only
      rw [← hget]
      exact pivot_value hs ho hc hφ hi
    | none =>
      simp only [Int.cast_zero, zero_mul, sum_const_zero]
      have hr := (allBelow_iff.mp hroles) s hs96
      rw [Bool.or_eq_true, Bool.or_eq_true, List.contains_iff_mem, List.contains_iff_mem] at hr
      rcases hr with (h | h) | h
      · obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := pos_of_mem h; rw [hf] at hj; exact absurd hj (by simp)
      · obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := pos_of_mem h; rw [hp] at hj; exact absurd hj (by simp)
      · have hl := ((slot_facts hs ho).1 s hs96).1
        exact hφ.1.1 (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) (by rw [fl_val hl]; exact h)

theorem phi_ind (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ}
    (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (corner o)) (n : ℕ) :
    φ (fl n) = (if touches (corner o) (n % 1024) = true then 1 else 0) *
      φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) (slotOf (corner o) (n % 1024)))) := by
  by_cases ht : touches (corner o) (n % 1024) = true
  · rw [if_pos ht, one_mul]; exact phi_touch hs ho n ht
  · rw [if_neg ht, zero_mul]; exact phi_untouch hφ n (by simpa using ht)

/-- **The κ bound on a class box**, from a valid certificate. -/
theorem kappa_class (hg : geomCheck = true) (hs : slotCheck = true) {o : ℕ} (ho : o < 16)
    {c : KCert} (hc : kappaCheck o c = true) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ} (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (corner o)) :
    500 * ∑ l, φ l ^ 2 ≤ 3321 * ∑ p, curl φ p ^ 2 := by
  have hsf := slot_facts hs ho
  have hgf := geom_facts hg
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ : ∃ v : ℕ → ℝ, v = fun s => φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ : ∃ w : ℕ → ℝ, w = fun j => v (c.free.getD j 0) := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  have hv' : ∀ s, v s = φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) := fun s => by rw [hv]
  have hw' : ∀ j, w j = v (c.free.getD j 0) := fun j => by rw [hw]
  -- the norm in slot coordinates
  have hnorm : ∑ l, φ l ^ 2 = ∑ s ∈ range 96, v s ^ 2 := by
    rw [show (∑ s ∈ range 96, v s ^ 2) = ∑ s ∈ range 96, φ (fl (slotLink (corner o) s)) ^ 2 from
      sum_congr rfl fun s _ => by rw [hv' s]]
    rw [sum_fin_eq_range (fun l => φ l ^ 2) (fun n => φ (fl n) ^ 2) (fun n h => by rw [fl_val h])]
    refine sum_range_eq_of_inj (slotLink (corner o)) (slotOf (corner o)) (touches (corner o)) (fun n => φ (fl n) ^ 2)
      (fun s hs' => ⟨(hsf.1 s hs').1, (hsf.1 s hs').2.2⟩) (fun n hn ht => hsf.2.1 n hn ht) ?_
    intro n hn ht
    show φ (fl n) ^ 2 = 0
    rw [phi_untouch hφ n (by rwa [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hn])]; ring
  -- the curvature over the patch
  have hcurv : ∑ p, curl φ p ^ 2 = ∑ q ∈ range 216, curl φ (flp (patchPlaq (corner o) q)) ^ 2 := by
    rw [sum_fin_eq_range (fun p => curl φ p ^ 2) (fun n => curl φ (flp n) ^ 2)
      (fun n h => by rw [flp_val h])]
    refine sum_range_eq_of_inj (patchPlaq (corner o)) (patchOf (corner o))
      (fun p => touches (corner o) (plaqLink p 0 % 1024) || touches (corner o) (plaqLink p 1 % 1024) ||
        touches (corner o) (plaqLink p 2 % 1024) || touches (corner o) (plaqLink p 3 % 1024))
      (fun n => curl φ (flp n) ^ 2) (fun q hq => hsf.2.2.1 q hq) ?_ ?_
    · intro p hp hP
      have key : ∀ i < 4, touches (corner o) (plaqLink p i % 1024) = true →
          patchOf (corner o) p < 216 ∧ patchPlaq (corner o) (patchOf (corner o) p) = p := by
        intro i hi ht
        obtain ⟨hmem, hlt⟩ := hgf.2.2.2.2.2 p hp i hi
        rw [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hlt] at ht
        obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := hsf.2.1 _ hlt ht
        exact hsf.2.2.2 _ h1 p (by rw [h2]; exact hmem)
      simp only [Bool.or_eq_true] at hP
      rcases hP with ((h | h) | h) | h
      · exact key 0 (by norm_num) h
      · exact key 1 (by norm_num) h
      · exact key 2 (by norm_num) h
      · exact key 3 (by norm_num) h
    · intro p hp hP
      simp only [Bool.or_eq_false_iff] at hP
      obtain ⟨⟨⟨h0, h1⟩, h2⟩, h3⟩ := hP
      show curl φ (flp p) ^ 2 = 0
      rw [flp_val hp]
      unfold curl
      simp only
      rw [phi_untouch hφ _ h0, phi_untouch hφ _ h1, phi_untouch hφ _ h2, phi_untouch hφ _ h3]
      ring
  -- the curvature at a patch slot is the local combination
  have hloc : ∀ q < 216, curl φ (flp (patchPlaq (corner o) q)) =
      ((dlocOf (corner o) q).map fun e => (e.2 : ℝ) * v e.1).sum := by
    intro q hq
    have hterm : ∀ i : ℕ, (((if touches (corner o) (plaqLink (patchPlaq (corner o) q) i % 1024) = true then
        (if i < 2 then 1 else -1) else 0 : ℤ)) : ℝ) *
          v (slotOf (corner o) (plaqLink (patchPlaq (corner o) q) i % 1024)) =
        (if i < 2 then 1 else -1) * φ (fl (plaqLink (patchPlaq (corner o) q) i)) := by
      intro i
      rw [phi_ind hs ho hφ, hv']
      split_ifs <;> simp
    rw [flp_val (hsf.2.2.1 q hq).1]
    unfold dlocOf
    rw [List.map_map, show List.range 4 = [0, 1, 2, 3] from rfl]
    simp only [List.map_cons, List.map_nil, List.sum_cons, List.sum_nil, Function.comp_apply]
    rw [hterm 0, hterm 1, hterm 2, hterm 3]
    unfold curl
    norm_num
    ring
  -- the coordinates of the slot vector in the fibre basis
  have hvZ : ∀ s < 96, v s = ∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (c.Z s j : ℝ) * w j :=
    fun s hs' => by
      rw [hv']; simp only [hw', hv']; exact slot_value hs ho hc hφ hs'
  have hKw : ∀ q < 216, ((dlocOf (corner o) q).map fun e => (e.2 : ℝ) * v e.1).sum =
      ∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (c.Kq (corner o) q j : ℝ) * w j := by
    intro q _
    unfold KCert.Kq
    rw [sum_list_comm]
    refine congrArg List.sum (List.map_congr_left fun e he => ?_)
    rcases dloc_slot hs ho q e he with h | h
    · simp [h]
    · rw [hvZ e.1 h]
  -- positivity of the certified form
  obtain ⟨_, hR, _, hB, hP⟩ := kappaCheck_parts hc
  obtain ⟨_, _, _, hwC, hwM, hK⟩ := kRanges_parts hR
  unfold kBound at hB
  rw [decide_eq_true_eq, KCert.βHk_eq] at hB
  simp only [natpow_eq] at hB
  unfold kPsd at hP
  rw [c.Hpk_eq hs ho] at hP
  have hpsd := qf_nonneg_of_psdScan (H := c.H (corner o)) (βH := c.βH) hK hwM
    (fun i _ j _ => c.H_symm (corner o) i j) (fun i _ j _ => c.abs_H_le hwC (corner o) i j) hB hP w
  have hqf : qf c.free.length (fun i j => (c.H (corner o) i j : ℝ)) w = 2 ^ c.sig *
      (3321 * ∑ q ∈ range 216, (∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (c.Kq (corner o) q j : ℝ) * w j) ^ 2 -
        500 * ∑ s ∈ range 96, (∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (c.Z s j : ℝ) * w j) ^ 2) := by
    have e : (fun i j => (c.H (corner o) i j : ℝ)) = fun i j => (2 : ℝ) ^ c.sig *
        (3321 * (∑ q ∈ range 216, (c.Kq (corner o) q i : ℝ) * c.Kq (corner o) q j) -
          500 * ∑ s ∈ range 96, (c.Z s i : ℝ) * c.Z s j) := by
      funext i j; unfold KCert.H; push_cast; ring
    rw [e, qf_lin, qf_gram, qf_gram]
  rw [hqf] at hpsd
  have hsig : (0 : ℝ) < 2 ^ c.sig := by positivity
  have hmain : 500 * ∑ s ∈ range 96, (∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (c.Z s j : ℝ) * w j) ^ 2 ≤
      3321 * ∑ q ∈ range 216, (∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (c.Kq (corner o) q j : ℝ) * w j) ^ 2 := by
    have := (mul_nonneg_iff_of_pos_left hsig).mp hpsd
    linarith
  rw [hnorm, hcurv]
  have e1 : ∑ s ∈ range 96, v s ^ 2 = ∑ s ∈ range 96, (∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (c.Z s j : ℝ) * w j) ^ 2 :=
    sum_congr rfl fun s hs' => by rw [hvZ s (mem_range.mp hs')]
  have e2 : ∑ q ∈ range 216, curl φ (flp (patchPlaq (corner o) q)) ^ 2 =
      ∑ q ∈ range 216, (∑ j ∈ range c.free.length, (c.Kq (corner o) q j : ℝ) * w j) ^ 2 :=
    sum_congr rfl fun q hq => by
      rw [hloc q (mem_range.mp hq), hKw q (mem_range.mp hq)]
  rw [e1, e2]
  exact hmain

end KappaClass

section KappaAll

theorem trL_lin (t y μ : ℕ) (hμ : μ < 4) : trL t (4 * y + μ) = 4 * trSite t y + μ := by
  unfold trL
  rw [show (4 * y + μ) / 4 = y by omega, show (4 * y + μ) % 4 = μ by omega]

theorem trL_lt (hg : geomCheck = true) {t l : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (hl : l < 1024) : trL t l < 1024 := by
  have := ((geom_facts hg).1 t ht (l / 4) (by omega)).2.1
  unfold trL; omega

theorem trL_trL (hg : geomCheck = true) {t l : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (hl : l < 1024) :
    trL t (trL t l) = l := by
  have h := ((geom_facts hg).1 t ht (l / 4) (by omega)).1
  unfold trL
  rw [show (4 * trSite t (l / 4) + l % 4) / 4 = trSite t (l / 4) by omega,
    show (4 * trSite t (l / 4) + l % 4) % 4 = l % 4 by omega, h]
  omega

theorem trP_lt (hg : geomCheck = true) {t p : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (hp : p < 1536) : trP t p < 1536 := by
  have := ((geom_facts hg).1 t ht (p / 6) (by omega)).2.1
  unfold trP; omega

theorem trP_trP (hg : geomCheck = true) {t p : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (hp : p < 1536) :
    trP t (trP t p) = p := by
  have h := ((geom_facts hg).1 t ht (p / 6) (by omega)).1
  unfold trP
  rw [show (6 * trSite t (p / 6) + p % 6) / 6 = trSite t (p / 6) by omega,
    show (6 * trSite t (p / 6) + p % 6) % 6 = p % 6 by omega, h]
  omega

theorem plaqLink_tr (hg : geomCheck = true) {t p : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (hp : p < 1536) (i : ℕ) :
    plaqLink (trP t p) i = trL t (plaqLink p i) := by
  have hs : p / 6 < 256 := by omega
  have hst := (geom_facts hg).1 t ht (p / 6) hs
  have hμ := planeMu_lt (p % 6)
  have hν := planeNu_lt (p % 6)
  unfold plaqLink trP
  dsimp only
  rw [show (6 * trSite t (p / 6) + p % 6) / 6 = trSite t (p / 6) by omega,
    show (6 * trSite t (p / 6) + p % 6) % 6 = p % 6 by omega]
  split_ifs
  · rw [trL_lin _ _ _ hμ]
  · rw [trL_lin _ _ _ hν, (hst.2.2 _ hμ).1]
  · rw [trL_lin _ _ _ hμ, (hst.2.2 _ hν).1]
  · rw [trL_lin _ _ _ hν]

theorem inBox_tr (hg : geomCheck = true) {t c x : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (hc : c < 256) (hx : x < 256) :
    inBox (trSite t c) (trSite t x) = inBox c x := by
  have hcx := (geom_facts hg).1 t ht x hx
  have hcc := (geom_facts hg).1 t ht c hc
  have hb : ∀ a, bit t a < 2 := fun a => by unfold bit; exact Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num)
  unfold inBox
  rw [(hcx.2.2 0 (by norm_num)).2, (hcx.2.2 1 (by norm_num)).2, (hcx.2.2 2 (by norm_num)).2,
    (hcx.2.2 3 (by norm_num)).2, (hcc.2.2 0 (by norm_num)).2, (hcc.2.2 1 (by norm_num)).2,
    (hcc.2.2 2 (by norm_num)).2, (hcc.2.2 3 (by norm_num)).2]
  have e : ∀ a, decide (((coord x a + 2 * bit t a) % 4 + 4 - (coord c a + 2 * bit t a) % 4) % 4 < 2)
      = decide ((coord x a + 4 - coord c a) % 4 < 2) := by
    intro a
    have h1 := coord_lt x a
    have h2 := coord_lt c a
    have h3 := hb a
    exact decide_eq_decide.mpr (by omega)
  rw [e 0, e 1, e 2, e 3]

theorem touches_tr (hg : geomCheck = true) {t c l : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (hc : c < 256) (hl : l < 1024) :
    touches (trSite t c) (trL t l) = touches c l := by
  have hst := (geom_facts hg).1 t ht (l / 4) (by omega)
  have hstep := (geom_facts hg).2.2.2.2.1 (l / 4) (by omega) (l % 4) (Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num))
  unfold touches trL
  rw [show (4 * trSite t (l / 4) + l % 4) / 4 = trSite t (l / 4) by omega,
    show (4 * trSite t (l / 4) + l % 4) % 4 = l % 4 by omega,
    (hst.2.2 _ (Nat.mod_lt _ (by norm_num))).1, inBox_tr hg ht hc (by omega),
    inBox_tr hg ht hc hstep]

/-- The translation by `2t` as a permutation of the links. -/
def trLink (t : ℕ) (l : Fin 1024) : Fin 1024 := fl (trL t l)

/-- The translation by `2t` as a permutation of the plaquettes. -/
def trPlaq (t : ℕ) (p : Fin 1536) : Fin 1536 := flp (trP t p)

theorem trLink_val (hg : geomCheck = true) {t : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (l : Fin 1024) :
    (trLink t l).val = trL t l := Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (trL_lt hg ht l.2)

theorem trLink_invol (hg : geomCheck = true) {t : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) :
    Function.Involutive (trLink t) := by
  intro l
  apply Fin.ext
  rw [trLink_val hg ht, trLink_val hg ht, trL_trL hg ht l.2]

theorem trPlaq_invol (hg : geomCheck = true) {t : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) :
    Function.Involutive (trPlaq t) := by
  intro p
  apply Fin.ext
  show trP t ((trP t p) % 1536) % 1536 = p
  rw [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (trP_lt hg ht p.2), trP_trP hg ht p.2, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt p.2]

theorem curl_tr (hg : geomCheck = true) {t : ℕ} (ht : t < 16) (φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ) (p : Fin 1536) :
    curl (fun l => φ (trLink t l)) p = curl φ (trPlaq t p) := by
  have hp' : (trPlaq t p).val = trP t p := Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (trP_lt hg ht p.2)
  have key : ∀ i < 4, trLink t (fl (plaqLink p i)) = fl (plaqLink (trPlaq t p) i) := by
    intro i hi
    have hlt := ((geom_facts hg).2.2.2.2.2 p p.2 i hi).2
    apply Fin.ext
    rw [trLink_val hg ht]
    show trL t (plaqLink p i % 1024) = plaqLink (trPlaq t p) i % 1024
    rw [hp', plaqLink_tr hg ht p.2, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hlt,
      Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (trL_lt hg ht hlt)]
  unfold curl
  beta_reduce
  rw [key 0 (by norm_num), key 1 (by norm_num), key 2 (by norm_num), key 3 (by norm_num)]

theorem fibre_tr (hg : geomCheck = true) {o t : ℕ} (ht : t < 16)
    {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ} (hφ : φ ∈ fibre (trSite t (corner o))) :
    (fun l => φ (trLink t l)) ∈ fibre (corner o) := by
  have hc : corner o < 256 := site4_lt _ _ _ _
  refine ⟨⟨fun l hl => ?_, fun r => ?_⟩, fun l hl => ?_⟩
  · apply hφ.1.1
    rw [trLink_val hg ht, (geom_facts hg).2.1 t ht l l.2]; exact hl
  · -- the translated pin row
    have hr : (r : ℕ) / 16 < 4 := by omega
    have hZ : ((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t < 16 :=
      Nat.xor_lt_two_pow (n := 4) (by omega) (by omega)
    have hr' : 16 * ((r : ℕ) / 16) + (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) < 64 := by omega
    have e1 : (16 * ((r : ℕ) / 16) + (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t)) % 16 = ((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t := by
      omega
    have e2 : (16 * ((r : ℕ) / 16) + (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t)) / 16 = (r : ℕ) / 16 := by omega
    rw [← hφ.1.2 ⟨_, hr'⟩]
    unfold pinSum
    simp only [e1, e2]
    refine sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
    have hbs : blockSite ((r : ℕ) % 16) i < 256 := site4_lt _ _ _ _
    have htb := (geom_facts hg).2.2.1 t ht ((r : ℕ) % 16) (by omega) i i.2
    have hst := (geom_facts hg).1 t ht _ hbs
    have hstep := (geom_facts hg).2.2.2.2.1 _ hbs _ hr
    have ha : trLink t (fl (4 * blockSite ((r : ℕ) % 16) i + (r : ℕ) / 16)) =
        fl (4 * blockSite (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) i + (r : ℕ) / 16) := by
      apply Fin.ext
      rw [trLink_val hg ht]
      show trL t ((4 * blockSite ((r : ℕ) % 16) i + (r : ℕ) / 16) % 1024) =
        (4 * blockSite (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) i + (r : ℕ) / 16) % 1024
      rw [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (by omega), trL_lin _ _ _ hr, htb]
      have := site4_lt (2 * bit (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) 0 + bit i 0)
        (2 * bit (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) 1 + bit i 1) (2 * bit (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) 2 + bit i 2)
        (2 * bit (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) 3 + bit i 3)
      unfold blockSite
      omega
    have hb' : trLink t (fl (4 * step (blockSite ((r : ℕ) % 16) i) ((r : ℕ) / 16) + (r : ℕ) / 16)) =
        fl (4 * step (blockSite (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) i) ((r : ℕ) / 16) + (r : ℕ) / 16) := by
      apply Fin.ext
      rw [trLink_val hg ht]
      show trL t ((4 * step (blockSite ((r : ℕ) % 16) i) ((r : ℕ) / 16) + (r : ℕ) / 16) % 1024) =
        (4 * step (blockSite (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) i) ((r : ℕ) / 16) + (r : ℕ) / 16) % 1024
      rw [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (by omega), trL_lin _ _ _ hr, ← (hst.2.2 _ hr).1, htb]
      have := (geom_facts hg).2.2.2.2.1 (blockSite (((r : ℕ) % 16) ^^^ t) i) (site4_lt _ _ _ _) _ hr
      omega
    rw [ha, hb']
  · apply hφ.2
    rw [trLink_val hg ht, touches_tr hg ht hc l.2]; exact hl

/-- **The κ bound for every box**, from valid certificates for the sixteen class boxes. -/
theorem kappa_of_certs (hg : geomCheck = true) (hs : slotCheck = true) (cs : ℕ → KCert)
    (hk : ∀ o < 16, kappaCheck o (cs o) = true) (b : Fin 256) {φ : Fin 1024 → ℝ}
    (hφ : φ ∈ fibre b) : ∑ l, φ l ^ 2 ≤ 3321 / 500 * ∑ p, curl φ p ^ 2 := by
  obtain ⟨hb, ho, ht⟩ := (geom_facts hg).2.2.2.1 b b.2
  set o := clsOf b
  set t := trOf b
  rw [← hb] at hφ
  have h := kappa_class hg hs ho (hk o ho) (fibre_tr hg ht hφ)
  have e1 : ∑ l, (fun l => φ (trLink t l)) l ^ 2 = ∑ l, φ l ^ 2 :=
    Equiv.sum_comp (Function.Involutive.toPerm _ (trLink_invol hg ht)) (fun l => φ l ^ 2)
  have e2 : ∑ p, curl (fun l => φ (trLink t l)) p ^ 2 = ∑ p, curl φ p ^ 2 := by
    simp only [curl_tr hg ht]
    exact Equiv.sum_comp (Function.Involutive.toPerm _ (trPlaq_invol hg ht))
      (fun p => curl φ p ^ 2)
  rw [e1, e2] at h
  linarith

end KappaAll


